WEBVTT


00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.353
BETHANY: I was born in Hawaii
to two die-hard surfers.


00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.364
How could I not have
salt water in my veins?


00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.732
They say home is
where the heart is.


00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:46.863
And for most people, that consists
of four walls and a welcome mat.


00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.567
But for me, it's the ocean.


00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.974
With the warmth
of the sun on my skin.


00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.342
(EXCLAIMING)


00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.619
"Two brothers."


00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.421
That's my answer when anyone
asks me why I'm so competitive.


00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.629
(LAUGHING)


00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.767
And, of course,
there's my best friend Alana.


00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.300
(GIGGLING)


00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.463
Trick or treat!
Trick or treat!


00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.973
(SINGING HELE ON TO KAUAI)


00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.652
We spent more time wet
than we did dry.


00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.288
My mom was convinced
that we were mermaids.


00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.068
From the moment
I caught my first wave,


00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.901
I knew that I wanted
to be a pro surfer.


00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.304
Nothing else seemed to matter.


00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.658
Surfing is my passion,
my way of life.


00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:18.395
The stoke I get from riding
a perfect wave is pure joy.


00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.169
But like my dad always says,
"Life is an adventure.


00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:33.471
"And sometimes, you wipe out and
end up in the impact zone."


00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:39.811
Bethany!


00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.616
Bethany!


00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.646
Let's go, you're lagging!


00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.753
I'm coming!


00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.454
Hey, sorry, Noah,
I lost track of time!


00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.395
(CHOIR SINGING HYMNS)


00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.408
Glad you could join us.


00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:13.213
Move over, Timmy.
Sorry, this seat's saved.


00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.617
Come on.
Ow!


00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.784
How were the waves?
Really fun.


00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.688
Ready for the contest?
Yeah.


00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.021
Practice your snap off the lip?
Shh.


00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.124
No, but she's perfect
on the wipeouts.


00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.993
Shh, guys, we're in church.


00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.429
She's going to do
her mermaid thing


00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:29.332
and crush it like
she always does.


00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.761
(ALL SINGING)


00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.621
(SINGING)


00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.665
(SINGING)


00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.017
(GIGGLES)


00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.753
NOAH: Almost got it.


00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:34.360
Darn it.


00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.194
Come on.


00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:41.934
Interesting technique, Noah.
Is that how the professionals do it?


00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.805
Hey, I know what I'm doing.


00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.709
Okay.


00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.541
Where you going?
To watch the competition.


00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:04.794
(EXCLAIMING JUBILANTLY)


00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:07.521
Whoa!


00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.589
(EXCLAIMING)


00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.300
(ALL WHOOPING)


00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:21.837
(ALL WHOOPING)


00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:27.042
(CHEERING)


00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.382
They gave me a five!


00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.289
Not so bad for a girl.


00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.831
(WHOOPING) Oh!


00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.300
(CHEERING)


00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:49.066
What!


00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:51.968
Read it and weep, honey.


00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:54.478
I'm not the one who's
going to be weeping.


00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:57.605
Five!


00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:58.809
Hey! Hey! Hey!


00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:00.010
Don't harass the judges!


00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.383
Hey! Hey! Hey!


00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:03.611
Hey!


00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.786
We're coming to get you!


00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.258
(LAUGHING)


00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:11.561
(GROANING)


00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.391
Babe, is it your knee again?


00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:14.455
Got you!


00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.758
(BARKING)


00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.626
(ALL SQUEALING)


00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:21.474
(SCREAMS) Noah, put me down!


00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:33.110
ANNOUNCER: Welcome, ladies and
gentlemen, to the junior portion


00:07:33.219 --> 00:07:36.086
of the Maui Jim Turtle Bay
Resort Invitational.


00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.385
We're expecting
a great competition today.


00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:40.221
We've got skateboarding
on the half-pipe.


00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.954
We've got all the action
in the water.


00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:43.427
Watch top amateur surf...


00:07:43.496 --> 00:07:44.485
Hey, howzit?


00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:45.724
Hey.
Hey, Keoki.


00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.265
If you get tired waiting
for the waves out there,


00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.960
you can always come
and kick it with us.


00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:50.127
We don't have to
wait for the action.


00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:52.364
Well, when you get tired of the
pipe, come surf some real waves.


00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:53.527
Ooh!


00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.230
Hey, Thursday night
is a full moon.


00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:58.334
If you guys aren't doing anything,
we're all gonna go surfing.


00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:00.038
Yeah, if we don't have
anything better to do.


00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:03.780
Okay.
See you guys later.


00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.010
All right. Bye.
Bye.


00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:12.386
ANNOUNCER: In semi-final heat number
one, we've got six competitors.


00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:14.289
In orange is Olivia Jenner.


00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.191
In black, Malina Birch.


00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:17.854
In blue, Bethany Hamilton.


00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.930
In yellow, Kaila Kahani.


00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:21.932
In white, Lalani Bri.


00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.764
And in pink, Alana Blanchard.


00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:24.894
(CHEERING)


00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:34.004
And it looks like the local groms have
tracked down Hawaiian surfing legend,


00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.172
Ben Aipa.


00:08:36.148 --> 00:08:37.342
Yeah, Ben!


00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:43.585
Hey, you see that
sick air Keoki just got?


00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:44.645
I don't think so.


00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.313
What?


00:08:46.392 --> 00:08:47.381
You're not going
to distract me.


00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:50.160
I'm catching that next wave.


00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:54.365
I don't think they know
how not to compete.


00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:55.730
Holt, you didn't
tell them, did you?


00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.166
No, no. I didn't want
to make them nervous.


00:08:57.270 --> 00:08:59.067
I'm nervous enough for the
both of them, as it is.


00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:00.833
You know, they both
have to place.


00:09:00.907 --> 00:09:02.704
ANNOUNCER: Black, Malina
Birch, you're in first.


00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.909
Blue, Bethany Hamilton,
you're in second


00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:07.411
looking for a 4.2
to overtake that top spot.


00:09:07.947 --> 00:09:09.608
Pink, Alana Blanchard,
you're in third,


00:09:09.682 --> 00:09:12.810
requiring a 5.4 to
overtake first place.


00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:14.477
Just a reminder,
ladies and gentlemen.


00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:16.545
The winners of today's
contest will qualify


00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.385
for the Hawaiian
Island Regionals.


00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:21.654
Alana Blanchard finds the
cover to finish things off.


00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.092
Solid wave for pink.


00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:24.355
Yes!


00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:26.225
Looks like we have
a paddle-battle here.


00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:27.556
Go, Bethany! Go!


00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:31.000
It's blue and black scratching
for a solid set wave.


00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.664
Malina Birch taking the inside
off of Bethany Hamilton.


00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:36.367
Here she is, up and riding.


00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:39.206
Malina Birch kicks things
off with a very nice ride.


00:09:39.278 --> 00:09:41.371
And a strong carve off the top.


00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:43.381
She definitely knows what
the judges are looking for.


00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:45.110
That will be a solid
wave for black.


00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:48.547
Malina full on stole my
wave, I had position.


00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:52.113
It's okay, it's all right.
Look, next time, I want you to really focus


00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:54.182
on just diving into the
water as far as you can.


00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.488
Rip that paddle
back. Okay?


00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:56.550
Okay.


00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:57.755
All right, take a rest.


00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.156
You thirsty?
Yeah.


00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.167
ANNOUNCER: With five minutes
remaining in this final,


00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:04.327
pink, Alana Blanchard,
you are in first.


00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.428
Black, Malina Birch,
you are in second.


00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:09.497
And blue, Bethany Hamilton,
you are currently in third.


00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:12.476
You're not breathing,
you know that, right?


00:10:18.184 --> 00:10:19.208
Go! Go!


00:10:27.793 --> 00:10:28.817
Yeah!


00:10:30.062 --> 00:10:31.586
ANNOUNCER:
Big snap off the top.


00:10:32.264 --> 00:10:34.494
She draws out
her second bottom turn,


00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:36.501
and hooks it one more time.


00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:38.969
Bethany Hamilton
is holding nothing back.


00:10:39.038 --> 00:10:41.529
Potentially one of the highest
scoring rides of the day.


00:10:41.741 --> 00:10:44.471
As this final comes to a
close here at Turtle Bay.


00:10:45.845 --> 00:10:48.678
(CROWD CHEERING) Yes!
That's what I'm talking about.


00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:51.180
You're doing a great job
training her, Brother Tom.


00:10:52.318 --> 00:10:53.307
Thanks, Ben.


00:10:53.386 --> 00:10:54.546
You got it, bro.


00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.917
Looks like she has
a real future.


00:10:56.355 --> 00:10:57.379
As a pro.


00:10:57.456 --> 00:10:59.321
She's been working so hard.


00:10:59.392 --> 00:11:01.383
Well, with her heart,
her will, she'll go far.


00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:08.123
ANNOUNCER: Third place of the Turtle Bay
Juniors final goes to Alana Blanchard.


00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:09.326
(CHEERING)


00:11:09.402 --> 00:11:11.632
In second place, Malina Birch.


00:11:12.505 --> 00:11:14.063
Good job, Malina.


00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:17.803
Meaning, taking first place
is Kauai's Bethany Hamilton.


00:11:17.877 --> 00:11:19.708
Bethany!
With today's big victory,


00:11:19.779 --> 00:11:22.179
Bethany Hamilton has to be
considered the favorite


00:11:22.248 --> 00:11:25.217
as we head to the
Hawaiian Island Regionals.


00:11:25.484 --> 00:11:26.815
(APPLAUSE)


00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:28.782
(WHOOPS)


00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:33.518
Way to go, Bethany.


00:11:34.593 --> 00:11:38.051
Girls, there's some people down
there you might want to meet.


00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.119
Who?


00:11:39.198 --> 00:11:41.166
It's the guys from Rip
Curl, it's no big deal.


00:11:41.233 --> 00:11:43.167
They want to sponsor
both of you.


00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:44.628
No way!
What!


00:11:44.704 --> 00:11:46.501
BOY: Oh, my gosh!
(SQUEALING EXCITEDLY)


00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:48.304
(GIGGLING)


00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.073
I got it, how about this one?


00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:55.045
Nice, if you're 100.


00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:56.103
Okay.


00:11:56.449 --> 00:11:57.473
What about this?


00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:58.539
Are you kidding?


00:11:59.151 --> 00:12:00.846
Thing looks like a eye patch.


00:12:01.821 --> 00:12:02.845
(MIMICS PIRATE SNARLING)


00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:04.881
I think it's hot.


00:12:05.725 --> 00:12:07.090
One wipeout in that tiny thing,


00:12:07.159 --> 00:12:10.720
and you're going to be showing a
lot more than your sick rides.


00:12:10.796 --> 00:12:12.661
Ooh, so much for so little.


00:12:13.099 --> 00:12:14.657
Well, good thing
it's on Rip Curl.


00:12:14.767 --> 00:12:15.756
Yes!


00:12:15.835 --> 00:12:16.824
(BOTH GIGGLE)


00:12:17.236 --> 00:12:19.067
ALANA: But make sure
to keep your eye on it,


00:12:19.138 --> 00:12:21.197
if you don't want it snaked
out from underneath you.


00:12:21.307 --> 00:12:22.672
Hey, girls.


00:12:22.942 --> 00:12:25.001
You realize I'm gonna take
you next time, right?


00:12:25.144 --> 00:12:26.873
Let's just let the
surfing do the talking.


00:12:28.414 --> 00:12:30.109
Every day between
now and regionals,


00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:31.774
when I'm in the water training,


00:12:31.851 --> 00:12:33.375
I'll be thinking
of you, Hamilton.


00:12:33.753 --> 00:12:35.243
Creepy.


00:12:35.321 --> 00:12:37.516
Thanks, but I think you should
stick to your training.


00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:39.217
Seems like you could
use a little focus.


00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:41.924
I guess we'll find out.


00:12:43.496 --> 00:12:44.724
Good seeing you again.


00:12:44.797 --> 00:12:45.821
(LAUGHS)


00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:54.506
You guys are usually the first
ones in here, let's go.


00:13:01.914 --> 00:13:03.848
SARAH: Let's finish up
Rad Night with a game.


00:13:03.916 --> 00:13:06.510
Can anyone tell me what
he or she thinks this is?


00:13:06.685 --> 00:13:07.811
Easy, it's a dodge ball.


00:13:07.887 --> 00:13:08.876
No.


00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:10.751
Or Mars?
Mmm-mmm.


00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:11.881
A blob in a lava lamp?


00:13:11.957 --> 00:13:12.946
(ALL LAUGH)


00:13:13.025 --> 00:13:14.890
Very creative, but no.


00:13:15.561 --> 00:13:17.028
It's a fly's eye.


00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:18.188
BOY: Weird.
GIRL: Ew!


00:13:18.264 --> 00:13:20.164
How about this one?
BYRON: A brain.


00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:22.024
Aren't brains
supposed to be pink?


00:13:22.101 --> 00:13:24.592
A dead, rotting brain?


00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:26.831
That is gross,
and that is a walnut.


00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.438
So, you see how hard it can
be to make sense of things


00:13:30.543 --> 00:13:33.307
when you're looking
at them really close?


00:13:33.379 --> 00:13:35.370
The same thing's true in life.


00:13:35.447 --> 00:13:37.278
So, if you guys are
dealing with anything,


00:13:37.349 --> 00:13:39.249
that's just too hard to handle


00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:41.650
or doesn't seem
to make much sense,


00:13:42.121 --> 00:13:43.452
get a new perspective.


00:13:43.856 --> 00:13:45.255
I want to share
with you guys something


00:13:45.324 --> 00:13:47.349
that has really made
an impact on my life.


00:13:47.459 --> 00:13:50.053
That's Jeremiah 29:11.


00:13:50.129 --> 00:13:53.064
"For I know the plans that I
have for you," says the Lord.


00:13:53.432 --> 00:13:55.923
"Plans to prosper you
and not to harm you.


00:13:56.035 --> 00:13:58.526
"Plans to give you
hope and a future."


00:13:59.939 --> 00:14:01.736
That's all the time
we have tonight, guys.


00:14:01.807 --> 00:14:03.570
If you are going
on the mission trip,


00:14:03.642 --> 00:14:06.338
please don't forget to give
me your permission slips.


00:14:08.881 --> 00:14:10.542
Hey, what's up?
What's this?


00:14:11.016 --> 00:14:13.917
Well, it looks like I'm not going
to be able to go to Mexico,


00:14:14.019 --> 00:14:15.987
so I brought some things
for the orphanage.


00:14:16.789 --> 00:14:18.313
I made the bracelets.


00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.416
Noah donated the shoes
and the Spam's from Timmy.


00:14:21.961 --> 00:14:23.451
Are you sure you can't come?


00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:27.198
Yeah, I've got to stay and
train now that I'm sponsored.


00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:29.527
I was really
looking forward to it.


00:14:29.602 --> 00:14:30.830
You're going to miss out.


00:14:33.005 --> 00:14:34.905
Well, have a good trip.


00:14:52.591 --> 00:14:53.956
Sarah's really bumming me out.


00:14:54.026 --> 00:14:55.254
Any particular reason?


00:14:55.327 --> 00:14:56.521
Yeah.


00:14:56.595 --> 00:14:59.291
So, I told her I'm not
coming to Mexico.


00:14:59.398 --> 00:15:00.831
I mean, she knows that I have


00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.460
two important competitions
coming up, right?


00:15:03.702 --> 00:15:05.499
I mean, she knows how much
I've put into this, you know?


00:15:06.105 --> 00:15:08.335
How much you and the whole
family has put into this.


00:15:08.407 --> 00:15:09.465
So what's her angle?


00:15:10.776 --> 00:15:13.142
That going to
Mexico to help kids


00:15:13.545 --> 00:15:15.206
is really important.


00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:18.273
And I know it is.
I mean, I really, really wish I could go.


00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.147
It's just,


00:15:20.219 --> 00:15:22.084
I've got to stay and
train for regionals.


00:15:22.154 --> 00:15:23.553
Did you say you'd go?


00:15:23.622 --> 00:15:26.716
Well, yeah, but that was
before I got sponsored.


00:15:27.159 --> 00:15:28.820
I mean, it's like
she's counting on me now,


00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:31.761
like I'm the only person in the
entire world who can do this.


00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.297
I mean, I'm not going.


00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:35.389
I mean, I can't, right?


00:15:35.467 --> 00:15:36.525
It's your call.


00:15:36.669 --> 00:15:39.797
(SIGHS) Great.
Now I feel even worse.


00:15:40.606 --> 00:15:44.042
That's good.
A small step in a good direction.


00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:04.191
The girls are all tucked in.


00:16:04.263 --> 00:16:07.255
How's it look tomorrow?
Pretty decent, actually.


00:16:08.133 --> 00:16:09.122
Well.


00:16:09.201 --> 00:16:10.327
No, no, no, you can't.


00:16:10.402 --> 00:16:11.426
What?


00:16:11.503 --> 00:16:12.492
You have your surgery tomorrow.


00:16:12.571 --> 00:16:14.038
The doctor said
no food after 10:00.


00:16:14.106 --> 00:16:15.232
This is like juice.


00:16:15.307 --> 00:16:16.467
Give it to me.
(CHUCKLING) No. No, no.


00:16:16.542 --> 00:16:17.804
Give it.
No.


00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:19.741
Give it. Give it.
No.


00:16:25.117 --> 00:16:27.415
ALANA: You need to relax, they'll
never know the difference.


00:16:27.486 --> 00:16:28.475
Maybe we shouldn't.


00:16:28.554 --> 00:16:30.749
I mean, we have to get up
super early for dawn patrol.


00:16:30.823 --> 00:16:31.812
I mean, what happens
if my mom comes in?


00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:33.790
Bethany, it'll be worth it.


00:16:33.859 --> 00:16:36.350
The moon's full.
The waves are perfect.


00:16:36.428 --> 00:16:39.625
I mean, come on, it's almost Halloween.
Even Noah's done it.


00:16:39.698 --> 00:16:41.598
He has?
Yeah.


00:16:41.667 --> 00:16:42.725
I really wanted to go.


00:16:42.801 --> 00:16:44.200
Shh! Okay,
come on, let's go.


00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:56.074
(ALL WHOOPING)


00:17:08.327 --> 00:17:09.726
(EXCLAIMING)


00:17:09.795 --> 00:17:11.126
(GIRLS GIGGLING)


00:17:13.866 --> 00:17:14.890
ALANA: Keoki.


00:17:14.967 --> 00:17:16.127
I knew it was you!


00:17:16.201 --> 00:17:17.293
KEOKI: No way!


00:17:17.369 --> 00:17:19.360
Yeah, you surf like a skater.


00:17:20.305 --> 00:17:21.738
Hey! (GIGGLES)


00:17:22.541 --> 00:17:23.565
(BOTH SCREAMING)


00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.845
You're toast, Keoki.


00:17:30.549 --> 00:17:31.538
Whoa!


00:17:35.854 --> 00:17:37.116
Okay, truce. Truce.


00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:38.178
Okay, deal.


00:17:39.625 --> 00:17:42.594
Bethy, it's almost midnight.


00:17:42.661 --> 00:17:44.356
What happens at midnight?


00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.419
You'll see.


00:17:47.666 --> 00:17:48.758
What?


00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:52.094
Later skater.


00:17:54.373 --> 00:17:55.965
(WHOOPING)


00:17:59.478 --> 00:18:00.672
(ALL CHEERING)


00:18:03.549 --> 00:18:04.777
How lucky are we?


00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:11.984
BETHANY: Awesome!


00:18:13.358 --> 00:18:14.689
(EXCLAIMING EXCITEDLY)


00:18:20.632 --> 00:18:21.894
(WHIRRING)


00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:25.092
Good morning.


00:18:25.204 --> 00:18:26.228
Morning.
Morning.


00:18:26.338 --> 00:18:28.431
So, as soon as you girls
get back from the water,


00:18:28.507 --> 00:18:30.441
I've got an English
assignment all ready for you.


00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:31.633
But it's a holiday.


00:18:31.743 --> 00:18:32.767
It's Halloween.


00:18:33.278 --> 00:18:34.643
We were thinking
that we could have


00:18:34.713 --> 00:18:36.180
a couple extra hours
on the waves today?


00:18:36.415 --> 00:18:37.746
'Cause you didn't get
enough last night?


00:18:38.317 --> 00:18:40.808
Just say the word and we can
enroll you girls in Kapa'a,


00:18:41.053 --> 00:18:42.953
where you can ride the bus
for 45 minutes each way


00:18:43.021 --> 00:18:45.717
and do eight hours of straight
work during prime surf hours.


00:18:45.791 --> 00:18:46.815
'Cause I'm all right with that.


00:18:47.693 --> 00:18:49.524
Actually, I love home school.


00:18:49.595 --> 00:18:51.563
Me, too.
Adore, totally.


00:18:52.431 --> 00:18:54.126
I'm really sorry, Mom.
It's just...


00:18:54.199 --> 00:18:57.168
I really, really wanted
to go night surfing.


00:18:57.236 --> 00:18:59.898
I mean, everyone talks
about how awesome it is.


00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:01.872
I mean, even Noah's done it.
He has?


00:19:02.174 --> 00:19:03.436
Good job.


00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.437
Why didn't you just ask?


00:19:06.512 --> 00:19:07.672
Because she knew you'd say no.


00:19:07.746 --> 00:19:08.735
How do you know I'd say no?


00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:09.803
Would you have let me go?


00:19:09.882 --> 00:19:11.873
No. I don't know.


00:19:12.251 --> 00:19:14.014
Hey, no, no, no, no.


00:19:15.187 --> 00:19:16.654
I promise I'll ask
next time, okay?


00:19:16.722 --> 00:19:17.814
I'm going to hold you to that.


00:19:18.157 --> 00:19:21.217
Dad, you should have them
upgrade you to a bionic knee


00:19:21.293 --> 00:19:23.158
so you can actually
beat Mom in surfing.


00:19:23.428 --> 00:19:25.487
It's going to take a lot
more than a bionic knee.


00:19:25.564 --> 00:19:27.225
You just wait.


00:19:27.299 --> 00:19:28.766
You sure you don't
want me to drive you?


00:19:28.834 --> 00:19:30.233
Mom, I got it.


00:19:30.636 --> 00:19:32.228
When you come through it,
I will be waiting.


00:19:32.437 --> 00:19:33.665
(HORN HONKING)


00:19:34.439 --> 00:19:35.838
That's your dad, Alana.
Have fun girls.


00:19:35.908 --> 00:19:36.966
ALANA: Bye.


00:19:37.042 --> 00:19:39.033
Bye, Dad. Say hi to
Dr. Rovinsky for me.


00:19:39.111 --> 00:19:40.510
Have a good surgery,
I'll be praying.


00:19:40.579 --> 00:19:43.104
Rip it up. See you
on the flip side.


00:19:43.582 --> 00:19:45.447
(UPBEAT SONG PLAYING)


00:19:51.256 --> 00:19:53.087
This is a good one.
This is a good song.


00:19:54.293 --> 00:19:56.420
Oh, that looks good,
doesn't it?


00:20:03.168 --> 00:20:04.533
All right, we're here.
Let's hit it.


00:20:04.603 --> 00:20:05.900
Let's get out.
Let's do it.


00:20:25.891 --> 00:20:28.655
Sweet. I've got
a meeting at 10:00,


00:20:28.727 --> 00:20:30.558
so we don't have
a lot of time today.


00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:33.427
No problem.
Just pick us up after your meeting.


00:20:33.498 --> 00:20:35.261
Yeah. Like that's
going to happen.


00:20:35.334 --> 00:20:36.926
Let's just get in
the water already.


00:20:37.002 --> 00:20:38.867
(WHOOPING) HOLT: Come on, it's
a long paddle around the reef.


00:20:38.937 --> 00:20:40.905
BETHANY:
Try and keep up with us.


00:20:42.174 --> 00:20:44.335
Well, the anesthetic should
have started working by now.


00:20:44.409 --> 00:20:45.398
You feel anything?


00:20:45.477 --> 00:20:47.445
A little bit.


00:20:47.512 --> 00:20:49.537
All right, it will
kick in shortly.


00:20:49.615 --> 00:20:53.176
We'll have you back out there shredding
waves with Bethany in no time.


00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:54.344
Thanks, David.


00:21:37.763 --> 00:21:38.855
Yeah!


00:21:52.878 --> 00:21:54.675
Whoa! Whoo!


00:21:56.014 --> 00:21:57.481
Did you see that one?


00:21:57.549 --> 00:21:59.312
That was nice
off the lip, buddy.


00:21:59.384 --> 00:22:00.373
Thanks.


00:22:02.621 --> 00:22:04.851
I wonder what bathing suit
I should wear to the shoot.


00:22:04.923 --> 00:22:08.086
The pink's cute, but the black
really works with my tan.


00:22:09.161 --> 00:22:10.788
I don't think
you get to decide.


00:22:10.862 --> 00:22:12.489
They'll probably just
tell us what to wear.


00:22:12.798 --> 00:22:14.891
I guess, but it's fun
to think about.


00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:21.367
Can you believe we get to
come out here every day?


00:22:21.573 --> 00:22:22.699
Yeah.


00:22:25.744 --> 00:22:26.768
(SCREAMING)


00:22:26.845 --> 00:22:28.107
ALANA: Dad!
Alana!


00:22:29.314 --> 00:22:30.338
ALANA: Shark!


00:22:31.416 --> 00:22:32.474
I need to get to the beach.


00:22:32.551 --> 00:22:33.575
Oh, God!


00:22:37.489 --> 00:22:39.047
BYRON: Dad,
where's the shark at?


00:22:39.124 --> 00:22:41.092
We need to get to the reef!
Just get to the reef.


00:22:57.309 --> 00:22:58.742
Keep on the board,
keep on the board.


00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:01.870
Byron, you get to shore!
Go! Go! Call 911!


00:23:03.348 --> 00:23:04.645
It's going to be okay, Beth.


00:23:05.817 --> 00:23:07.284
I'll start it for you!


00:23:09.888 --> 00:23:12.083
Come on. Ready, pal? Let's go.
Push, push, push.


00:23:12.157 --> 00:23:13.419
(GRUNTING)


00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:21.492
HOLT: Stay with us, sweetie, okay?
Stay with us.


00:23:21.566 --> 00:23:23.591
Please, Jesus. Please...


00:23:24.035 --> 00:23:25.525
Alana, you keep her on the board.
Okay.


00:23:25.604 --> 00:23:27.231
On the board.
Please get me to the beach.


00:23:27.305 --> 00:23:28.294
Please.


00:23:29.908 --> 00:23:31.569
You're going to be okay!


00:23:33.578 --> 00:23:34.602
(BYRON PANTING)


00:23:44.156 --> 00:23:45.180
Come on!


00:23:53.899 --> 00:23:55.264
(DIALING)


00:23:58.303 --> 00:24:00.168
All right, here we go.


00:24:01.606 --> 00:24:02.971
Doctor Rovinsky,
we need this room stat!


00:24:03.041 --> 00:24:05.236
It's a teenage girl from the North Shore.
Shark attack.


00:24:06.645 --> 00:24:08.909
Who? Who is it?


00:24:09.047 --> 00:24:11.174
I'll check it out, Tom.
I'll check it out.


00:24:15.787 --> 00:24:17.652
HOLT: Stay with me,
Bethany!


00:24:20.859 --> 00:24:21.883
(RETCHING)


00:24:24.296 --> 00:24:25.729
Alana! Get over here!


00:24:25.797 --> 00:24:27.196
ALANA: (CRYING) I can't.


00:24:29.434 --> 00:24:30.901
Morning, Mom.


00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:33.900
When did you go night surfing?


00:24:33.972 --> 00:24:35.303
(CELL PHONE RINGING)


00:24:35.373 --> 00:24:38.001
Uh...
Night surfing...


00:24:39.778 --> 00:24:42.076
All right.
All right, sweetheart.


00:24:42.147 --> 00:24:43.239
Ambulance is coming, all right?


00:24:43.315 --> 00:24:44.339
I want my mom.


00:24:44.416 --> 00:24:46.213
I know. We're gonna get your mom.
We're gonna get your mom.


00:24:46.318 --> 00:24:48.218
Wait, wait, wait. What?


00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:53.314
Mom?


00:24:53.525 --> 00:24:55.755
Dad! I called 911!
I called her mom.


00:24:55.827 --> 00:24:56.885
Okay, okay, okay.


00:24:56.962 --> 00:24:57.986
Grab the foot
of the board. Okay?


00:24:58.063 --> 00:25:01.032
Grab it, on the count of three.
Ready? One, two, three!


00:25:01.099 --> 00:25:02.123
Go, go, go, go, go!


00:25:02.267 --> 00:25:04.064
Take her up to the truck!
Let's get her up there right now!


00:25:04.135 --> 00:25:05.261
Come on. Talk to me.


00:25:05.337 --> 00:25:06.599
(GRUNTING)


00:25:10.542 --> 00:25:12.100
(ALANA CRYING)


00:25:12.844 --> 00:25:14.641
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)


00:25:15.280 --> 00:25:16.975
Watch your step right here!
What your step right there!


00:25:17.048 --> 00:25:18.572
(DISTORTED VOICES)


00:25:19.117 --> 00:25:20.379
Where's the ambulance, Dad?
They're not here yet!


00:25:20.452 --> 00:25:22.750
Don't worry about the ambulance!
We'll meet it on the way!


00:25:22.821 --> 00:25:24.015
BYRON: Alana,
get the board!


00:25:24.089 --> 00:25:26.580
Get her up! All right.
Get up, get up there!


00:25:42.641 --> 00:25:44.609
Bethany, can you hear me?
Oh, my God.


00:25:44.676 --> 00:25:46.041
She's losing
a lot of blood, Dad!


00:25:46.111 --> 00:25:47.476
(SIREN WAILING)


00:25:47.979 --> 00:25:49.378
All right, I see the ambulance.
Here it comes!


00:25:49.581 --> 00:25:50.639
(HONKING)


00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:53.244
(TIRES SCREECH)


00:25:55.453 --> 00:25:57.284
Who are you, sir?
Family friend.


00:25:57.355 --> 00:25:59.414
Do you know if she hit her head
or ever lost consciousness?


00:25:59.491 --> 00:26:01.049
No, she never passed out, but
she's lost a lot of blood.


00:26:01.126 --> 00:26:03.356
Here we go!
Careful! Easy.


00:26:04.095 --> 00:26:05.084
Okay, lock her in.


00:26:05.163 --> 00:26:06.460
Please don't die.


00:26:06.531 --> 00:26:08.158
Come on, come on,
come on, sweetie.


00:26:09.301 --> 00:26:10.700
(SIREN WAILING)


00:26:30.021 --> 00:26:31.613
(SHUDDERING)


00:26:34.426 --> 00:26:36.860
Please don't take her!
Please don't take her.


00:26:37.462 --> 00:26:38.520
Please don't take her.


00:26:43.435 --> 00:26:44.595
Tom, it's Bethany.


00:26:45.604 --> 00:26:46.593
No, no! No!


00:26:46.671 --> 00:26:47.695
Get me out of here!


00:26:47.772 --> 00:26:49.433
Get me out of here! No.
Come on. You can't move!


00:26:49.507 --> 00:26:50.496
Just let me get out of here!


00:26:50.575 --> 00:26:51.564
You can't walk!


00:26:51.643 --> 00:26:52.632
Get me out of here!
No!


00:26:53.845 --> 00:26:55.335
(SIREN WAILING)


00:26:56.648 --> 00:26:59.378
Talk to me. Gotta stay with me.
Keep looking at my eyes, okay?


00:27:01.353 --> 00:27:02.479
Where's my family?


00:27:02.554 --> 00:27:04.351
They're on their way.
They're gonna meet us at the hospital.


00:27:06.791 --> 00:27:08.315
She's going into
hypovolemic shock.


00:27:08.393 --> 00:27:09.382
(MONITOR BLEEPING)
We're almost there.


00:27:13.832 --> 00:27:14.890
Breathe deep.


00:27:24.476 --> 00:27:25.602
Mom, the car!


00:27:26.645 --> 00:27:27.907
Stay with me.


00:27:27.979 --> 00:27:29.105
Cheri, it happened so fast...


00:27:31.016 --> 00:27:32.608
PARAMEDIC: Traumatic amputation.
Severe loss of blood.


00:27:32.684 --> 00:27:33.844
CHERI: I'm here, baby,
I'm right here.


00:27:33.918 --> 00:27:35.886
Blood pressure 70 over 40 and dropping.
I'm right here.


00:27:35.954 --> 00:27:37.683
DOCTOR: Up, up!
Get her in here. Move!


00:27:37.756 --> 00:27:39.485
Come on!
Follow it back.


00:27:40.025 --> 00:27:41.014
Let's go!
Stay with us!


00:27:41.092 --> 00:27:42.286
NOAH: Hang in there.
Bethany, you'll be okay!


00:27:42.360 --> 00:27:43.486
CHERI: What's happening?


00:27:43.561 --> 00:27:45.256
(VOICES DISTORTING)


00:27:50.001 --> 00:27:50.990
Get her in a bed.


00:27:51.069 --> 00:27:52.195
NURSE:
Move her into bay three!


00:27:52.270 --> 00:27:53.897
PARAMEDIC: Come on, Bethany.
Stay with us, stay with us.


00:27:53.972 --> 00:27:54.961
CHERI: What's happening?


00:27:55.040 --> 00:27:56.064
NURSE: Bethany!


00:27:56.675 --> 00:27:58.142
(INAUDIBLE)


00:28:56.801 --> 00:28:58.826
(MONITOR BEEPING STEADILY)


00:29:14.586 --> 00:29:15.644
Mom?


00:29:17.122 --> 00:29:19.590
Hi, sweetheart.
I'm right here.


00:29:23.461 --> 00:29:24.519
TOM: Hey.


00:29:24.763 --> 00:29:25.889
We're all here.


00:29:26.531 --> 00:29:27.589
It hurts.


00:29:28.433 --> 00:29:29.491
Okay.


00:29:29.567 --> 00:29:30.556
Noah, get the doctor.


00:29:30.635 --> 00:29:32.296
Yeah, I got it.


00:29:35.140 --> 00:29:36.232
I'm a little thirsty.


00:29:36.307 --> 00:29:37.501
Okay.
Got it.


00:29:40.011 --> 00:29:41.603
(INHALES DEEPLY)


00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:45.378
Dad, please don't cry.


00:29:45.817 --> 00:29:47.079
(CRYING)


00:29:47.152 --> 00:29:48.676
I'm not crying.


00:29:49.687 --> 00:29:51.450
I'm going to be okay.


00:29:51.689 --> 00:29:52.883
I know.


00:29:55.593 --> 00:29:57.060
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)


00:29:57.862 --> 00:30:00.387
Hey there, kiddo.


00:30:01.232 --> 00:30:02.665
How you holding up?


00:30:03.301 --> 00:30:04.700
Pretty good, thanks to you.


00:30:06.137 --> 00:30:08.537
I guess I ruined
your surf shirt, huh?


00:30:09.908 --> 00:30:11.899
Well, I never liked
that one anyway.


00:30:13.411 --> 00:30:16.141
Why don't you just concentrate
on getting better, okay?


00:30:19.517 --> 00:30:20.575
Thank you.


00:30:26.024 --> 00:30:28.083
You were amazing out there.


00:30:29.093 --> 00:30:31.118
You were the one
who kept me calm.


00:30:31.196 --> 00:30:32.254
You never...


00:30:32.931 --> 00:30:34.023
You never let go.


00:30:36.267 --> 00:30:38.497
You are incredibly
brave, Bethany.


00:30:40.104 --> 00:30:41.162
Where's Alana?


00:30:43.374 --> 00:30:46.741
She's... She's at home.
With her mother.


00:30:46.811 --> 00:30:47.903
She's...


00:30:48.780 --> 00:30:50.247
She's still
a little freaked out.


00:30:52.016 --> 00:30:53.574
But, you know, she'll be better


00:30:53.651 --> 00:30:55.084
knowing that you're
going to be okay.


00:30:55.153 --> 00:30:56.279
So...


00:31:00.425 --> 00:31:01.449
DR. ROVINSKY: Hey.


00:31:02.327 --> 00:31:03.419
How's my favorite patient?


00:31:03.828 --> 00:31:05.295
BETHANY: You say
that to everyone.


00:31:05.897 --> 00:31:06.989
I mean it when I see you.


00:31:07.699 --> 00:31:09.564
I'll wait outside.
I'll see you later.


00:31:09.934 --> 00:31:12.767
So, I understand you're
feeling some discomfort.


00:31:12.837 --> 00:31:13.826
Yeah.


00:31:13.905 --> 00:31:15.202
Well, that's normal.


00:31:15.340 --> 00:31:19.208
There's going to be a lot of pain
because of the trauma that you endured.


00:31:19.277 --> 00:31:22.542
Not to mention the fact that you've
lost over 60% of your blood.


00:31:22.981 --> 00:31:26.314
You're going to be feeling kind of
lousy for the next few days, kid.


00:31:27.452 --> 00:31:29.682
Now here's the thing, Bethany.


00:31:30.221 --> 00:31:35.318
The things that you're going to have to
learn to do differently is extensive.


00:31:35.393 --> 00:31:36.917
But the good news.


00:31:36.995 --> 00:31:38.622
Those things you're not
gonna be able to do


00:31:39.197 --> 00:31:40.459
is small.


00:31:42.467 --> 00:31:44.230
I'm so proud of you.


00:31:52.510 --> 00:31:53.807
I'll tell you something.


00:31:54.479 --> 00:31:56.572
She is a living miracle.


00:31:58.149 --> 00:31:59.309
Thanks, David.


00:32:13.865 --> 00:32:14.957
Hey, sleepy head.


00:32:15.033 --> 00:32:16.022
Hi.


00:32:21.172 --> 00:32:22.764
How you feeling?


00:32:24.142 --> 00:32:25.166
I've been better.


00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:30.645
When can I surf again?


00:32:32.350 --> 00:32:33.840
Are you busy right now?


00:32:34.852 --> 00:32:35.876
Kind of.


00:32:39.724 --> 00:32:40.816
Soon.


00:32:42.193 --> 00:32:43.785
How do you know?


00:32:46.230 --> 00:32:49.688
Because you can
do all things...


00:32:49.801 --> 00:32:51.632
Through him who
gives me strength.


00:32:51.703 --> 00:32:54.137
...through him who
gives me strength.


00:33:04.983 --> 00:33:06.746
Noah, eat your food.


00:33:07.585 --> 00:33:09.883
It's gross.
I'm not hungry.


00:33:09.988 --> 00:33:11.012
Eat it. Mine's fine.


00:33:11.389 --> 00:33:13.380
I said, I'm not hungry.


00:33:14.325 --> 00:33:16.657
Well, if you didn't want it, why'd
you let me pay for it then?


00:33:17.061 --> 00:33:18.528
Fine.
I'll pay you back.


00:33:19.731 --> 00:33:21.028
I think you two
should calm down.


00:33:21.232 --> 00:33:22.290
I am calm.


00:33:22.367 --> 00:33:23.356
We're not doing this.


00:33:23.434 --> 00:33:24.423
NOAH: Doing what?


00:33:25.136 --> 00:33:26.262
Life's got to go on


00:33:26.337 --> 00:33:27.895
the way it's always gone on.
What you talking about?


00:33:27.972 --> 00:33:29.940
Life is not going to go on the
way it has always gone on.


00:33:30.008 --> 00:33:31.873
Will you stop arguing?
No, he's arguing with me.


00:33:31.943 --> 00:33:33.342
TIMMY: Everyone's
yelling at everyone.


00:33:33.411 --> 00:33:34.708
TOM: Stop it.
Stop it!


00:33:53.164 --> 00:33:54.927
(BREATHING HEAVILY)


00:33:58.803 --> 00:33:59.861
(SCREAMS)


00:34:02.306 --> 00:34:04.900
Hey, sweetheart. It's a dream, okay?
Just a dream, that's all.


00:34:05.476 --> 00:34:06.738
Just a dream.


00:34:06.811 --> 00:34:08.244
(SOBBING) It wasn't a dream!


00:34:09.113 --> 00:34:10.205
It was real.


00:34:10.515 --> 00:34:11.504
(SOBBING)


00:34:11.682 --> 00:34:14.708
You should go see her.
You know that?


00:34:16.187 --> 00:34:18.246
You need to go see her.


00:34:20.291 --> 00:34:22.816
...was resting on her surfboard
in the ocean off Hawaii,


00:34:22.894 --> 00:34:26.159
when, suddenly,
a shark bites off her arm.


00:34:26.664 --> 00:34:31.067
The girl doesn't even scream, and her
composure may have saved her life.


00:34:31.135 --> 00:34:32.625
(SWITCHES OFF TV) You're
pretty much on every channel.


00:34:33.471 --> 00:34:34.665
Hey!


00:34:35.540 --> 00:34:37.167
Where have you been?


00:34:37.241 --> 00:34:39.209
You know, at home,
living it up.


00:34:52.356 --> 00:34:53.653
How have you been?


00:35:05.036 --> 00:35:06.867
(TEARFULLY) I thought you
were going to die out there.


00:35:23.588 --> 00:35:27.115
So, are you still going to do
that Rip Curl photo shoot?


00:35:28.192 --> 00:35:29.682
They wanted me to.


00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:31.625
But I told them I couldn't
do it without you.


00:35:31.696 --> 00:35:33.323
But that's crazy.


00:35:33.397 --> 00:35:35.456
You've been nuts for that shoot.
You have to do it.


00:35:36.267 --> 00:35:37.256
Really?


00:35:37.535 --> 00:35:39.230
Yeah. Of course.


00:35:39.604 --> 00:35:40.764
Do it for both of us.


00:36:04.629 --> 00:36:07.860
CHERI: You're not going to believe
how great the house smells.


00:36:08.900 --> 00:36:11.698
Plants are everywhere.


00:36:11.769 --> 00:36:13.134
More flowers
have been delivered


00:36:13.204 --> 00:36:14.796
than there are growing
on the entire island.


00:36:15.006 --> 00:36:16.974
Dr. Rovinsky said
that I can get back


00:36:17.041 --> 00:36:19.373
in the water as soon
as my stitches come out.


00:36:20.745 --> 00:36:22.042
Can we try a shower first?


00:36:37.562 --> 00:36:39.792
That's so cool.
Who did that?


00:36:39.864 --> 00:36:40.853
Everybody.


00:36:42.099 --> 00:36:44.499
The bite on Bethany
Hamilton's surfboard


00:36:44.569 --> 00:36:47.197
was 16 inches long
and 8 inches wide.


00:36:47.305 --> 00:36:49.967
...currently searching for a
shark believed to be responsible


00:36:50.041 --> 00:36:52.236
for the attack on
Bethany Hamilton.


00:36:52.310 --> 00:36:53.299
CHERI: It's okay.


00:36:53.377 --> 00:36:54.366
(HONKING)


00:36:56.614 --> 00:36:58.241
NOAH: Hey! Hey! Hey!


00:36:59.050 --> 00:37:00.347
Hey! Get out of here!


00:37:00.418 --> 00:37:01.476
BETHANY: Where's Dad?


00:37:01.552 --> 00:37:02.746
Bethany!


00:37:02.820 --> 00:37:04.185
(CLAMORING)
(CAMERAS CLICKING)


00:37:08.392 --> 00:37:09.723
I said leave!


00:37:09.994 --> 00:37:11.188
Noah! Noah!


00:37:11.262 --> 00:37:12.752
Just get back in the house.
Dad...


00:37:12.830 --> 00:37:13.922
Unlock the back door.


00:37:13.998 --> 00:37:15.625
Bethany, is this...
Come on, get out of my way!


00:37:15.700 --> 00:37:17.861
Excuse me! Pardon me!
Excuse me! Excuse me.


00:37:18.102 --> 00:37:19.433
I've got it from here,
honey. Scoot over.


00:37:19.503 --> 00:37:20.800
What are you gonna do?


00:37:44.028 --> 00:37:45.791
Nice driving, 007.


00:37:45.863 --> 00:37:48.297
You know what?
I never liked those bushes anyway, Dad.


00:37:48.366 --> 00:37:50.095
NOAH: Come on, Bethany,
I got you.


00:37:50.167 --> 00:37:52.032
Give me your bag.
I didn't know you could drive like that.


00:37:52.937 --> 00:37:53.995
Neither did I.


00:37:58.609 --> 00:38:00.406
So what do we do now?


00:38:00.911 --> 00:38:04.039
Remember when we brought
Noah home from the hospital?


00:38:04.115 --> 00:38:07.141
He was our first baby and
we had no clue what to do.


00:38:08.085 --> 00:38:09.985
It's the same thing.


00:38:10.054 --> 00:38:12.045
We'll take it day by day.


00:38:21.565 --> 00:38:23.157
(CAMERAS CLICKING)


00:38:23.234 --> 00:38:24.633
That's so messed up.


00:38:24.702 --> 00:38:26.033
I wish they would go away.


00:38:27.672 --> 00:38:29.299
(GINGER BARKING)


00:38:29.974 --> 00:38:31.999
Ginger! Hi, girl!


00:38:33.411 --> 00:38:34.503
Oh!


00:38:34.578 --> 00:38:36.170
I know, I know, I know.


00:38:37.715 --> 00:38:38.875
I know. It's still me.


00:38:39.784 --> 00:38:41.046
Ginger!


00:38:41.519 --> 00:38:42.543
(LAUGHS)


00:38:42.787 --> 00:38:44.755
Who's up for sandwiches?


00:38:45.923 --> 00:38:48.323
Sounds so good, I'm starving.


00:38:48.392 --> 00:38:49.984
CHERI: Noah?
Yeah, sure.


00:38:52.697 --> 00:38:54.392
Okay, where's my Spam?


00:38:54.732 --> 00:38:55.721
Mexico.


00:38:56.033 --> 00:38:57.022
All of it?


00:39:00.638 --> 00:39:01.696
CHERI: I got it.
I got it, sweetie.


00:39:02.173 --> 00:39:03.538
Sorry, Mom.
It's okay.


00:39:19.390 --> 00:39:20.857
Here, let me grab that.


00:39:20.925 --> 00:39:22.187
You want to get
some bread, love?


00:39:22.259 --> 00:39:23.351
Yeah.


00:39:31.736 --> 00:39:32.862
Um...


00:39:33.671 --> 00:39:35.298
I need to go unpack.


00:39:35.373 --> 00:39:36.362
Are you sure?
Uh-huh.


00:39:56.594 --> 00:39:57.993
(STRUMMING)


00:40:18.682 --> 00:40:19.910
TOM: I have some
good news to share.


00:40:20.117 --> 00:40:21.141
What news?


00:40:21.585 --> 00:40:24.383
Holt got a call from that
show, Inside Edition,


00:40:25.356 --> 00:40:28.120
and they want to give
Bethany a prosthetic arm.


00:40:28.192 --> 00:40:30.285
Wait, wait, wait.
She's been home for five minutes.


00:40:30.361 --> 00:40:31.419
They're gonna pay
for the entire thing.


00:40:31.495 --> 00:40:32.860
When did you talk to a TV show?


00:40:32.930 --> 00:40:34.158
And it's custom made.


00:40:34.832 --> 00:40:36.823
Will it look normal?


00:40:36.901 --> 00:40:38.198
I would think so.


00:40:38.269 --> 00:40:39.736
Awesome.


00:40:39.837 --> 00:40:41.031
Can they make one
I can surf with?


00:40:41.105 --> 00:40:42.163
What does she have to do?


00:40:42.239 --> 00:40:45.538
All she has to do is give a brief
interview, wearing the arm.


00:40:45.609 --> 00:40:48.271
Check out my sister
the celebrity.


00:40:48.345 --> 00:40:49.676
You don't have to do this.


00:40:49.747 --> 00:40:51.977
No. I want to.


00:40:53.484 --> 00:40:55.008
Yeah, yeah, I'll do it.


00:40:55.085 --> 00:40:56.677
So, it's settled.


00:40:57.321 --> 00:40:59.516
Hey, wait.
Let's give thanks.


00:41:22.646 --> 00:41:24.637
BETHANY: That arm could
not come soon enough.


00:41:24.715 --> 00:41:26.512
Because trying to
make do with only one,


00:41:27.084 --> 00:41:29.052
even harder than it sounds.


00:41:29.119 --> 00:41:31.849
I mean, fixing your hair is
not exactly rocket science.


00:41:31.922 --> 00:41:33.947
Unless you've only got one arm.


00:41:34.024 --> 00:41:36.458
Then it might as well
be a mission to Mars.


00:41:36.527 --> 00:41:39.189
Every day of my life, for as
far back as I could remember,


00:41:39.263 --> 00:41:40.662
I was in the water.


00:41:40.731 --> 00:41:44.030
And now, I couldn't even
put my bathing suit on.


00:41:44.201 --> 00:41:46.863
Almost everything
seemed to be a challenge.


00:41:46.937 --> 00:41:51.101
But what scared me most, was that I
might not be able to surf again.


00:41:58.749 --> 00:41:59.909
(WHISPERING) It's so sad.


00:42:13.197 --> 00:42:15.927
Mommy, what happened
to that girl's arm?


00:42:17.234 --> 00:42:18.326
I'm sorry.


00:42:22.506 --> 00:42:23.700
CHERI: Should I go?


00:42:23.774 --> 00:42:25.833
Or do you want to do this together?
It's up to you.


00:42:26.977 --> 00:42:28.001
Stay.


00:42:31.148 --> 00:42:32.240
Okay.


00:42:37.288 --> 00:42:38.346
Oh, it's looking great.


00:42:40.024 --> 00:42:42.424
It's healing nicely.
You all right?


00:42:45.763 --> 00:42:47.230
There you go.


00:42:52.736 --> 00:42:55.034
It's going to look better
once the stitches are out.


00:43:05.482 --> 00:43:06.915
(DOOR SHUTS)


00:43:10.888 --> 00:43:12.219
(SIGHING)


00:43:29.673 --> 00:43:31.072
Is she okay?


00:43:33.410 --> 00:43:34.672
You okay?


00:43:34.745 --> 00:43:35.973
(CRYING)


00:43:52.029 --> 00:43:54.759
Hey! I just got
back from Mexico.


00:43:54.832 --> 00:43:57.892
I'm so glad you're okay.


00:43:57.968 --> 00:44:00.368
I was just about
to come see you.


00:44:00.437 --> 00:44:02.029
I couldn't wait.


00:44:02.106 --> 00:44:03.437
Come here.


00:44:04.441 --> 00:44:08.878
I was thinking about you, and
praying for you every minute.


00:44:08.946 --> 00:44:10.345
How are you?


00:44:10.414 --> 00:44:11.506
Oh...


00:44:11.815 --> 00:44:15.478
I'm good. Yeah.
Everyone's been doing really good.


00:44:18.255 --> 00:44:20.689
You don't have to
do that, Bethany.


00:44:20.758 --> 00:44:22.123
Not with me.


00:44:24.161 --> 00:44:25.719
(SIGHING) Um...


00:44:26.163 --> 00:44:28.825
They're trying
to help. I know.


00:44:29.633 --> 00:44:30.827
I know.


00:44:32.636 --> 00:44:34.194
But...


00:44:36.607 --> 00:44:37.869
But what?


00:44:41.512 --> 00:44:46.848
You know how you said it's hard
to see things clearly sometimes


00:44:46.917 --> 00:44:48.544
when you're too close?
Mmm-hmm.


00:44:50.387 --> 00:44:54.517
Well, I've been trying
to get some perspective.


00:44:55.192 --> 00:44:56.557
I've been really trying.


00:45:07.071 --> 00:45:08.197
(SOBBING)


00:45:08.706 --> 00:45:13.871
Sarah, how can this be
God's plan for me?


00:45:13.944 --> 00:45:15.673
I don't understand.


00:45:15.846 --> 00:45:17.040
(SOBBING)


00:45:22.119 --> 00:45:25.953
I don't know why terrible
things happen to us sometimes.


00:45:27.624 --> 00:45:31.492
But I have to believe that something
good is going to come out of this.


00:45:32.262 --> 00:45:33.456
Okay.


00:45:33.530 --> 00:45:35.259
I don't know what that is.


00:45:37.134 --> 00:45:38.897
I really wish I did.


00:45:40.404 --> 00:45:41.735
Come here.


00:45:51.215 --> 00:45:52.910
(PHONE RINGING)


00:45:52.983 --> 00:45:54.143
Hello?


00:45:55.686 --> 00:45:56.744
Dad.


00:45:59.189 --> 00:46:00.520
Excuse us.


00:46:29.019 --> 00:46:31.044
That's a perfect fit, bro.


00:46:40.464 --> 00:46:41.931
TIMMY:
Come on, Dad.


00:47:10.694 --> 00:47:12.525
Hey, Alana, can you take
a little half step forward?


00:47:12.596 --> 00:47:14.530
Put your hand a little
higher on the board.


00:47:14.598 --> 00:47:16.691
That is gorgeous.
Perfect.


00:47:19.403 --> 00:47:20.734
Beautiful.


00:47:22.005 --> 00:47:24.803
You're natural born
for this. Gorgeous.


00:47:26.443 --> 00:47:28.206
Absolutely gorgeous.


00:47:31.148 --> 00:47:32.706
(BOYS WHOOPING)


00:47:39.356 --> 00:47:41.187
PHOTOGRAPHER: Actually, Alana,
go take a break, come back,


00:47:41.258 --> 00:47:42.748
grab a new bikini,
that'd be perfect.


00:47:48.966 --> 00:47:50.297
So? How did I look?


00:47:50.367 --> 00:47:51.493
Great.


00:47:52.135 --> 00:47:53.329
Not too cheesy, right?


00:47:53.637 --> 00:47:54.763
Uh...


00:47:54.905 --> 00:47:57.237
Somewhere between cheddar
and jalapeno jack.


00:47:58.075 --> 00:47:59.975
(LAUGHS SARCASTICALLY)


00:48:01.111 --> 00:48:02.169
Thank you.


00:48:05.349 --> 00:48:07.579
That guy's ripping
it up out there, yeah?


00:48:07.651 --> 00:48:08.640
Yeah.


00:48:08.719 --> 00:48:10.118
Hey, Alana, we're ready
for you over here!


00:48:12.856 --> 00:48:15.381
You know, you should
be doing this with me.


00:48:16.727 --> 00:48:17.785
No.


00:48:18.362 --> 00:48:19.590
You should.


00:48:21.031 --> 00:48:22.293
Go on, they're waiting for you.


00:48:22.366 --> 00:48:23.424
(EXCLAIMS IN FRUSTRATION)


00:48:23.500 --> 00:48:24.694
Don't worry about me.


00:48:37.547 --> 00:48:39.879
She's right,
you should listen to her.


00:48:41.318 --> 00:48:42.842
Yeah, and you should
stop listening


00:48:42.920 --> 00:48:46.151
to other people's
conversations, you kook.


00:48:46.223 --> 00:48:47.781
Just got your back.


00:48:47.858 --> 00:48:48.950
Loser.


00:48:49.026 --> 00:48:50.050
Poser.


00:48:53.864 --> 00:48:56.662
You should be out there
with her, though.


00:48:59.369 --> 00:49:01.462
Yeah, I should be with her.


00:49:03.173 --> 00:49:04.697
Just not there.


00:49:08.512 --> 00:49:10.343
TIMMY: What's
taking so long?


00:49:17.654 --> 00:49:19.451
NOAH: So what's
for breakfast?


00:49:20.590 --> 00:49:21.955
Wouldn't you like to know?


00:49:22.059 --> 00:49:23.822
Yeah, we would.
We're hungry! Yes!


00:49:26.496 --> 00:49:27.485
(BLOWS)


00:49:27.831 --> 00:49:29.958
Mmm.
(MIMICKING FANFARE)


00:49:30.801 --> 00:49:32.428
Okay.
What's the occasion?


00:49:33.804 --> 00:49:36.830
Does there have to be an occasion
for me to make my family


00:49:36.907 --> 00:49:39.501
fresh squeezed orange juice
and homemade banana bread?


00:49:40.978 --> 00:49:43.708
You do realize that tomorrow is
Thanksgiving, not today, right?


00:49:43.947 --> 00:49:46.541
Yeah. That's why
it's the perfect time.


00:49:47.017 --> 00:49:48.075
Perfect time for what?


00:49:49.519 --> 00:49:50.679
To get back in the water.


00:50:07.871 --> 00:50:09.532
Aren't you afraid?


00:50:10.507 --> 00:50:12.236
I'm more afraid of not surfing.


00:50:12.309 --> 00:50:15.540
All right, get out there and
have some fun! (WHOOPS)


00:50:17.447 --> 00:50:18.675
Come on.


00:50:19.383 --> 00:50:20.577
Come on, let's go already!


00:50:24.988 --> 00:50:26.478
Are you ready?


00:50:27.190 --> 00:50:28.384
If she is, I am.


00:50:35.365 --> 00:50:37.492
Grab my ankle,
I'll tow you out.


00:50:37.567 --> 00:50:38.556
No, I'm good.


00:50:42.873 --> 00:50:44.340
There you go!


00:50:45.375 --> 00:50:47.502
Just take it nice
and easy, Bethany.


00:50:52.015 --> 00:50:55.143
Hey, don't worry about it.
It was a junk wave anyway.


00:50:55.218 --> 00:50:57.345
Yeah, I'll get the next one.


00:51:01.858 --> 00:51:02.882
Ooh!


00:51:02.959 --> 00:51:03.948
(COUGHING)


00:51:04.928 --> 00:51:07.726
CHERI: Why don't you
just paddle today?


00:51:07.798 --> 00:51:09.425
No.


00:51:09.499 --> 00:51:10.488
We can come back tomorrow.


00:51:10.567 --> 00:51:11.625
No, I'm good.


00:51:16.440 --> 00:51:18.908
Try putting your hand in
the center of the board,


00:51:19.009 --> 00:51:21.307
along the stringer
so you don't tip over.


00:51:26.817 --> 00:51:28.182
(COUGHING)


00:51:28.652 --> 00:51:30.119
Be patient, honey.


00:51:44.801 --> 00:51:46.359
Yes!
(WHOOPING)


00:51:46.436 --> 00:51:47.630
Look at that!
Yeah!


00:51:51.341 --> 00:51:52.899
(ALL WHOOPING)


00:51:53.577 --> 00:51:54.771
(LAUGHING) Yeah!


00:51:54.845 --> 00:51:56.369
(CHEERING)


00:51:59.649 --> 00:52:00.673
(SCREAMING)


00:52:01.384 --> 00:52:02.908
(ALL EXCLAIMING)


00:52:07.090 --> 00:52:09.115
Yeah!


00:52:09.192 --> 00:52:12.457
That's the way to go, honey!


00:52:12.529 --> 00:52:14.053
Got it all on camera.


00:52:14.131 --> 00:52:15.462
Training starts tomorrow.


00:52:15.532 --> 00:52:16.829
Training for what?


00:52:16.933 --> 00:52:18.093
The Hawaiian Island Regionals.


00:52:22.239 --> 00:52:24.503
(UPBEAT HAWAIIAN
MUSIC PLAYING)


00:52:25.509 --> 00:52:27.409
(INAUDIBLE)


00:52:36.553 --> 00:52:37.884
TOM: Excuse me!


00:52:38.588 --> 00:52:40.453
Happy Thanksgiving, everyone.


00:52:40.524 --> 00:52:41.923
ALL: Happy Thanksgiving!


00:52:41.992 --> 00:52:43.357
Thanks so much for coming.


00:52:43.426 --> 00:52:46.554
And if you don't mind, I'd like
to offer up a little toast.


00:52:46.630 --> 00:52:47.995
Sweetheart.


00:52:49.599 --> 00:52:54.298
We are so blessed and thankful
to God for all of you


00:52:54.871 --> 00:52:55.929
because of your love


00:52:56.606 --> 00:52:59.404
and your support
over the past few weeks.


00:53:00.610 --> 00:53:04.444
And we are especially thankful to be
spending yet another Thanksgiving


00:53:04.548 --> 00:53:06.607
with our sweet,
beloved daughter.


00:53:07.217 --> 00:53:08.275
Here's to Bethany!


00:53:08.652 --> 00:53:10.085
ALL: To Bethany!


00:53:10.420 --> 00:53:11.751
(ALL CHEERING)


00:53:14.591 --> 00:53:15.717
That was embarrassing.


00:53:15.792 --> 00:53:17.191
I thought it was wonderful.


00:53:18.628 --> 00:53:20.095
Hey!
Hey!


00:53:20.163 --> 00:53:21.425
I heard you're
back in the water.


00:53:21.498 --> 00:53:22.897
I know, and there's
something else.


00:53:22.966 --> 00:53:24.399
Oh, yeah?
Uh-huh.


00:53:25.101 --> 00:53:26.830
I'm surfing the Hawaiian
Island Regionals.


00:53:26.903 --> 00:53:28.530
Are you kidding me?
No!


00:53:28.605 --> 00:53:30.038
Oh, my gosh, that's so amazing!


00:53:30.106 --> 00:53:31.664
Bethany, I am so proud of you!


00:53:31.741 --> 00:53:32.730
Thanks.


00:53:33.009 --> 00:53:35.500
Well, you really outdid yourself
again this year, Cheri.


00:53:35.579 --> 00:53:37.513
I helped.
He tasted everything.


00:53:37.581 --> 00:53:40.311
Yeah, one of my many talents.
Like clearing the table.


00:53:40.383 --> 00:53:42.146
Let me help you.
Thank you.


00:53:46.223 --> 00:53:49.590
I realize this would be a very
different day without you.


00:53:50.860 --> 00:53:53.158
You know, I just wish
I could have done more.


00:53:54.297 --> 00:53:57.494
Our family is a family
because of you.


00:54:04.474 --> 00:54:07.307
TODD: We have made this to
your exact specifications.


00:54:07.377 --> 00:54:09.174
Doesn't it look real?


00:54:11.081 --> 00:54:14.073
Yeah. That's kind of
weird how real it looks.


00:54:14.184 --> 00:54:18.314
And you can even
paint the fingernails.


00:54:19.723 --> 00:54:20.951
Shall we try it on?


00:54:25.228 --> 00:54:27.753
Now, you just take that strap,
and I'll take this one.


00:54:27.831 --> 00:54:29.128
(BARKING)


00:54:29.199 --> 00:54:30.564
Hold tight.


00:54:32.636 --> 00:54:34.365
There, how does that feel?


00:54:34.437 --> 00:54:35.461
It's okay.


00:54:35.538 --> 00:54:36.527
(SNAPS)


00:54:36.606 --> 00:54:37.595
(BARKS)


00:54:38.408 --> 00:54:41.206
Let me just see how
it works on my board.


00:54:47.017 --> 00:54:48.314
Not weight bearing.


00:54:48.385 --> 00:54:50.546
How am I supposed to use
it to push up on my board?


00:54:50.654 --> 00:54:52.588
I think you might have to
do that with the other arm.


00:54:52.656 --> 00:54:54.886
So, is there a way I can
grab the rails to duck dive?


00:54:55.358 --> 00:54:57.724
Honey, why don't you
just give it a chance?


00:54:57.794 --> 00:54:59.762
How am I supposed to paddle
and surf in this thing?


00:55:00.397 --> 00:55:01.421
I mean, look at it!


00:55:01.731 --> 00:55:02.993
Yeah.


00:55:03.066 --> 00:55:06.126
TODD: Because the remainder
of your arm is so short,


00:55:06.202 --> 00:55:10.332
mobility will be limited.


00:55:10.640 --> 00:55:11.902
But there's so much
more you can do...


00:55:11.975 --> 00:55:13.203
Can I take it off, please?


00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:14.607
TODD: Every single thing...
CHERI: Take it off.


00:55:14.678 --> 00:55:17.238
She said she wants you to take it off.
You can turn that off.


00:55:18.682 --> 00:55:19.808
(BARKING)


00:55:19.883 --> 00:55:21.908
Hey! No! Hey!
Don't! Hey! Drop it!


00:55:21.985 --> 00:55:23.543
Ginger!
TIMMY: Drop it! Ginger, stop!


00:55:23.620 --> 00:55:24.678
Drop it!
TIMMY: No. Release!


00:55:24.754 --> 00:55:26.415
Honey, you can still
surf without it.


00:55:26.489 --> 00:55:27.615
TIMMY: Let it go!
NOAH: Ginger!


00:55:27.691 --> 00:55:28.749
Bad dog!
Ginger!


00:55:28.825 --> 00:55:29.849
Bad dog!


00:55:43.306 --> 00:55:45.069
CHERI: I like her
better that way.


00:55:50.480 --> 00:55:52.345
Dad was right.


00:55:53.083 --> 00:55:54.641
I don't need it to surf.


00:55:54.718 --> 00:55:56.208
No, you don't.


00:56:03.226 --> 00:56:05.194
Would it be better to
just say it out loud?


00:56:08.998 --> 00:56:10.397
I thought...


00:56:11.735 --> 00:56:14.568
I thought at least with clothes
on, I could have two arms.


00:56:16.873 --> 00:56:18.738
Thought I could look normal.


00:56:19.342 --> 00:56:21.310
Normal is so overrated.


00:56:21.378 --> 00:56:22.902
But people like normal, Mom.


00:56:23.380 --> 00:56:24.779
Who?
Guys do.


00:56:25.281 --> 00:56:26.976
(INHALING SHARPLY)


00:56:27.751 --> 00:56:29.446
I mean, who will even
like me with this?


00:56:30.320 --> 00:56:34.620
The right guy will love you
exactly the way you are.


00:56:35.558 --> 00:56:37.526
Because you're beautiful.


00:56:37.961 --> 00:56:39.053
How do you know?


00:56:39.963 --> 00:56:41.487
Because I know.


00:56:44.868 --> 00:56:47.302
What's that worth,
right? Nothing.


00:56:49.339 --> 00:56:50.328
(SIGHS)


00:56:56.579 --> 00:56:58.911
What are you doing?


00:56:58.982 --> 00:57:02.543
We had this statue in my house,
when I was a little girl.


00:57:03.153 --> 00:57:06.589
It was a replica from a museum
my parents once went to.


00:57:06.656 --> 00:57:09.022
I didn't even think
about it until just now.


00:57:10.093 --> 00:57:11.583
BETHANY: Venus de Milo.


00:57:12.328 --> 00:57:14.125
For centuries,
all around the world,


00:57:14.230 --> 00:57:17.063
she was considered
the pinnacle of beauty.


00:57:19.669 --> 00:57:22.103
And she has one
less arm than you.


00:57:25.475 --> 00:57:27.272
Yeah, but I can surf.


00:57:29.879 --> 00:57:30.971
(GRUNTS)


00:57:31.047 --> 00:57:32.878
So, regionals.


00:57:32.949 --> 00:57:35.747
What we have to do is
to get you from here


00:57:38.955 --> 00:57:41.150
to here.


00:57:41.224 --> 00:57:42.486
It's not going to be easy.


00:57:43.359 --> 00:57:45.953
I don't need easy,
I just need possible.


00:57:47.831 --> 00:57:50.595
With you, anything's possible.


00:57:52.202 --> 00:57:53.226
Let's do it.


00:58:03.980 --> 00:58:05.311
(INAUDIBLE)


00:58:15.758 --> 00:58:16.952
Right there.
On the take off.


00:58:17.026 --> 00:58:18.323
Right there. Now, look.
A little back step.


00:58:18.394 --> 00:58:19.383
Yeah.


00:58:19.462 --> 00:58:21.396
That could be a sign...
'Cause that time I wiped out.


00:58:29.539 --> 00:58:31.063
Just a hair late
when you take off.


00:58:32.308 --> 00:58:35.072
So, I'll just adjust my body so
that my weight is even more...


00:58:35.144 --> 00:58:36.736
Or bring your arm all
the way around. Yes.


00:58:40.550 --> 00:58:41.949
(INAUDIBLE)


00:59:00.136 --> 00:59:01.933
Look at her. That's it.
That's it, right there!


00:59:02.005 --> 00:59:03.472
That is perfect.
Okay.


00:59:03.540 --> 00:59:05.371
That's what you want to
go for every time. Yup.


00:59:13.616 --> 00:59:15.049
How'd you feel out
there this morning?


00:59:15.818 --> 00:59:19.652
Pretty good. I mean, I have a little
trouble getting under the big waves,


00:59:19.756 --> 00:59:21.246
but once I'm up, I'm solid.


00:59:24.193 --> 00:59:26.923
I'll come in if I can't
handle it, okay?


00:59:29.465 --> 00:59:30.625
(SPEAKING HAWAIIAN)


00:59:30.700 --> 00:59:32.099
Good morning.
I'm Piper Borraow.


00:59:32.168 --> 00:59:33.157
And I'm Rob Bucannan.


00:59:33.236 --> 00:59:36.103
And we'd like to welcome you to
the Hawaiian Island Regionals.


00:59:55.058 --> 00:59:56.685
How do you feel?


00:59:56.759 --> 00:59:57.817
Like barfing.


00:59:57.894 --> 00:59:59.759
Yeah, well, aim for Malina.


00:59:59.896 --> 01:00:02.262
If you don't want to do
this, you don't have to.


01:00:02.332 --> 01:00:03.993
I'm not going to pull out now.


01:00:04.067 --> 01:00:06.467
Besides everyone
knows I've entered.


01:00:06.536 --> 01:00:07.560
It's now or never.


01:00:07.637 --> 01:00:09.832
Soledad O'Brian is
in Phuket, Thailand.


01:00:09.906 --> 01:00:13.069
She has been following
efforts by some survivors


01:00:13.142 --> 01:00:15.201
to find their
missing loved ones.


01:00:15.278 --> 01:00:17.405
Hey, Bethany. Good luck
out there today, yeah.


01:00:17.480 --> 01:00:18.674
Thanks.


01:00:19.215 --> 01:00:20.773
Man, that's really awful.


01:00:20.850 --> 01:00:23.944
FEMALE REPORTER: Clearly, wherever you
look along the path of this tsunami


01:00:24.020 --> 01:00:27.046
there is just stories of loss,
and thousands already...


01:00:27.123 --> 01:00:29.114
I hope you guys get
a lot of donations.


01:00:29.192 --> 01:00:31.092
Yeah, Sarah's organizing a trip
to help the kids in Thailand.


01:00:31.160 --> 01:00:32.149
(HORN SOUNDING)


01:00:32.228 --> 01:00:34.822
My heat's coming up,
I gotta go. Bye.


01:00:36.899 --> 01:00:38.264
Great to have you
back, Bethany.


01:00:38.334 --> 01:00:40.529
Thanks, it's good to be back.


01:00:42.805 --> 01:00:45.137
So you're actually
going through with this?


01:00:45.208 --> 01:00:46.300
Yeah.


01:00:53.016 --> 01:00:54.381
MAN: Hey, Bethany.
BETHANY: Hey.


01:00:54.450 --> 01:00:57.180
Judges have approved giving
you a five minute head start.


01:01:02.492 --> 01:01:04.187
I don't want it.
Bethany.


01:01:05.028 --> 01:01:06.620
I don't need it.


01:01:08.731 --> 01:01:09.993
Okay.


01:01:17.707 --> 01:01:19.197
(CROWD CHEERING)


01:01:30.386 --> 01:01:31.375
Come on, Bethany.


01:01:31.688 --> 01:01:32.780
PIPER:
First heat has started


01:01:32.855 --> 01:01:35.551
and the girls are making their
way out into the lineup.


01:01:51.741 --> 01:01:54.471
All right, we've got Bethany
Hamilton in the blue jersey


01:01:54.544 --> 01:01:56.205
trying to catch her first wave.
(CHEERING)


01:01:56.546 --> 01:01:57.911
See ya!


01:01:59.182 --> 01:02:01.412
Bethany unable to
get into that wave.


01:02:01.484 --> 01:02:04.112
Meanwhile, Malina Birch
scratches into one.


01:02:04.187 --> 01:02:06.052
Looks like a good one.


01:02:08.391 --> 01:02:09.756
ROB: All right,
Malina Birch dropped in


01:02:09.826 --> 01:02:11.623
on that inside roll,
nice bottom turn.


01:02:11.694 --> 01:02:13.594
Off the bottom, coming up.


01:02:14.063 --> 01:02:15.121
Comes around the corner,


01:02:15.198 --> 01:02:17.029
gets a nice vertical
off the top there


01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:18.260
(CHEERING)


01:02:18.935 --> 01:02:20.527
As she kicks out
to the challengers.


01:02:21.671 --> 01:02:23.070
PIPER: Hamilton drops
into a nice looking wave.


01:02:23.139 --> 01:02:24.299
(ALL CHEERING)


01:02:24.907 --> 01:02:27.467
Ooh! A little loss
of control there.


01:02:27.977 --> 01:02:30.741
But nice recovery.
She cuts back into the white water.


01:02:31.013 --> 01:02:33.607
Should be a decent scoring
ride for the surfer in blue.


01:02:34.550 --> 01:02:35.778
(CHEERING)


01:02:50.933 --> 01:02:53.333
All right, Alana Blanchard,
drops into a wave of her own,


01:02:53.402 --> 01:02:56.235
nice off the bottom,
big snap off the top.


01:02:56.305 --> 01:02:59.502
Sets up again for a nice cut
back into the white water.


01:03:00.576 --> 01:03:03.170
Speeding down the line


01:03:03.346 --> 01:03:05.541
looking for a little tube
section, gets in there.


01:03:05.615 --> 01:03:08.743
Threads that little
barrel and exits.


01:03:09.452 --> 01:03:11.784
Nice wave for Alana Blanchard.


01:03:11.921 --> 01:03:14.321
All right, Rockwell, it looks
like at the ten minute mark


01:03:14.390 --> 01:03:18.827
we have Malina Birch in first
with a 7.3 on her first ride.


01:03:19.228 --> 01:03:21.696
(PANTING) Alana Blanchard
is second with a 6.2.


01:03:21.764 --> 01:03:23.994
And in third place,
Leila Hurst with a 5.3.


01:03:24.066 --> 01:03:25.090
The surf is picking up.


01:03:25.168 --> 01:03:27.693
Whoa, look at that outside,
a big set approaching.


01:03:27.770 --> 01:03:29.567
It looks like Bethany Hamilton
is going to get caught


01:03:29.639 --> 01:03:32.437
inside of the biggest
wave of the day.


01:03:32.875 --> 01:03:34.137
Come on, Bethany.
Come on!


01:03:39.615 --> 01:03:42.083
Mountains of water rolling
through here at Sunset Beach


01:03:42.151 --> 01:03:44.415
and it looks like our competitor
in blue, Bethany Hamilton,


01:03:44.487 --> 01:03:46.148
just taking some donuts out there.
(COUGHING)


01:03:49.625 --> 01:03:51.593
No! I'm fine!


01:03:52.061 --> 01:03:53.358
I knew she wouldn't come in.


01:04:00.970 --> 01:04:03.336
Bethany, grab my leash, I'll pull
you the rest of the way out.


01:04:03.406 --> 01:04:06.466
No, I'm fine.
I can do this!


01:04:08.611 --> 01:04:09.703
Come on, Bethany!


01:04:09.779 --> 01:04:10.939
PIPER: All right,
four minutes left,


01:04:11.013 --> 01:04:13.914
and Bethany Hamilton still
stuck in the impact zone, Rob.


01:04:13.983 --> 01:04:15.746
Bethany, in sixth
place, right now.


01:04:15.818 --> 01:04:17.308
She's still needing
quite a score.


01:04:17.386 --> 01:04:18.819
She's okay.


01:04:21.691 --> 01:04:24.751
Malina, don't!
You have enough, let her have it!


01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:33.264
ROB: Alana Blanchard just
dropped in on Malina Birch.


01:04:36.205 --> 01:04:37.502
(GROANS)


01:04:38.908 --> 01:04:41.843
That's definitely going to be an
interference call on Blanchard.


01:04:41.911 --> 01:04:43.936
PIPER: Alana Blanchard will
not make it on this heat,


01:04:44.013 --> 01:04:46.345
has been disqualified
for the interference.


01:04:46.916 --> 01:04:47.905
(INDISTINCT)


01:04:59.595 --> 01:05:00.584
(GASPING)


01:05:05.568 --> 01:05:07.661
I can't take it anymore, I want
you to get her out of there.


01:05:07.737 --> 01:05:08.726
I want her out of there.


01:05:08.804 --> 01:05:09.964
The lifeguards are on it.


01:05:10.039 --> 01:05:12.030
ROB: Oh, man, it looks
like she broke her board.


01:05:12.108 --> 01:05:13.905
PIPER: Well, unfortunately
for Bethany Hamilton,


01:05:13.976 --> 01:05:16.672
a broken board right now,
puts her in a bad position,


01:05:16.746 --> 01:05:18.213
with only 3 minutes remaining,


01:05:18.281 --> 01:05:21.842
there's no chance she's making
it out of this first heat.


01:05:24.253 --> 01:05:25.982
You shouldn't have dropped
in on Malina like that.


01:05:26.055 --> 01:05:28.023
She was trying...
She was just hassling me,


01:05:28.090 --> 01:05:29.079
like she always does.


01:05:29.158 --> 01:05:30.147
She's a jerk!


01:05:30.226 --> 01:05:32.421
At least she was treating me
like I was real competition.


01:05:32.528 --> 01:05:34.120
(CAMERAS CLICKING) Bethany,
what happened to you out there?


01:05:34.530 --> 01:05:35.758
Bethany.


01:05:36.465 --> 01:05:38.023
Can we please just
get out of here?


01:05:38.100 --> 01:05:39.931
NOAH: Make a path!
Get out of the way!


01:05:40.069 --> 01:05:41.559
(CLAMORING)


01:05:46.575 --> 01:05:48.270
(CLAMORING CEASES)


01:05:49.979 --> 01:05:51.003
(CAMERAS CLICKING)


01:05:51.080 --> 01:05:52.877
Stay calm. REPORTER: Bethany,
how are you feeling?


01:05:52.949 --> 01:05:54.849
That's enough, come on.


01:05:54.917 --> 01:05:56.282
(CHATTERING)


01:05:56.852 --> 01:05:58.820
Bethany, I know
that you got beat up


01:05:58.888 --> 01:06:00.378
pretty bad out there
today, sweetheart.


01:06:00.456 --> 01:06:01.753
But you can't
let it get you down.


01:06:01.824 --> 01:06:04.486
Enough, Dad, okay?
I can't do this anymore!


01:06:04.560 --> 01:06:05.754
Yes, you can, honey.


01:06:05.828 --> 01:06:07.090
Listen to her.


01:06:11.734 --> 01:06:13.793
GIRL: Bethany!
Bethany! Bethany!


01:06:13.869 --> 01:06:16.565
Hey, Bethany!
Can I get your autograph?


01:06:20.042 --> 01:06:22.670
I have something
even better actually.


01:06:32.955 --> 01:06:34.422
Here.


01:06:34.490 --> 01:06:35.479
Cool!


01:06:35.558 --> 01:06:37.321
Bethany, what are you doing?


01:06:39.462 --> 01:06:41.896
GIRL: Oh, my God!
This is so cool!


01:06:43.899 --> 01:06:45.833
Awesome, thanks!


01:06:45.901 --> 01:06:46.890
Enjoy them.


01:06:59.382 --> 01:07:00.371
Bethany.


01:07:00.449 --> 01:07:02.713
Dad, just stop. Okay?


01:07:03.652 --> 01:07:04.641
It's over.


01:07:15.564 --> 01:07:17.555
CHERI: That's not
what I'm saying.


01:07:17.633 --> 01:07:18.998
You can't give up on her.


01:07:19.068 --> 01:07:21.059
And you can't keep
pushing at her.


01:07:21.837 --> 01:07:24.203
What are you supposed to
do, just let her quit?


01:07:24.273 --> 01:07:25.433
If she wants to, yes.


01:07:25.508 --> 01:07:27.442
That's the most ridiculous
thing I've ever heard.


01:07:27.510 --> 01:07:29.000
Then you're not hearing
what I'm saying.


01:07:29.078 --> 01:07:31.706
What? What is it
that I'm not hearing?


01:07:31.781 --> 01:07:34.875
You can't always fix
everything by sheer will.


01:07:34.950 --> 01:07:36.918
Sometimes there is no...
(INCREASES VOLUME)


01:07:36.986 --> 01:07:38.954
ANNOUNCER: ...Hamilton has to
be considered the favorite


01:07:39.021 --> 01:07:41.114
as we head to the
Hawaiian Island Regionals.


01:07:41.390 --> 01:07:42.550
She's a surfer.


01:07:42.625 --> 01:07:43.751
She's a competitor.


01:07:43.826 --> 01:07:45.054
She's more than that.


01:07:45.127 --> 01:07:47.721
Cheri, if she walks
away from this...


01:07:48.364 --> 01:07:51.265
If she quits, she may never
get back in the water again.


01:07:51.333 --> 01:07:53.392
And she will never be the same.


01:07:53.669 --> 01:07:56.763
She will never be the same.


01:07:58.674 --> 01:08:02.405
And if she thinks the only life
out there for her is surfing


01:08:02.478 --> 01:08:03.911
and she can't make that happen


01:08:03.979 --> 01:08:05.913
then she's going to be lost.


01:08:06.182 --> 01:08:08.412
Really, really lost.


01:08:29.772 --> 01:08:33.606
Go ahead, tell me how
everything's going to be okay.


01:08:37.480 --> 01:08:40.813
Yeah, that's me. Mister
jump-right-in-and-fix-it.


01:08:44.453 --> 01:08:48.150
If I could just keep
my mouth shut for once.


01:08:49.692 --> 01:08:51.489
I'm done, aren't I?


01:08:54.029 --> 01:08:57.590
I can't even paddle out to the
lineup past the big waves.


01:08:58.701 --> 01:09:00.430
I don't understand.


01:09:02.338 --> 01:09:05.569
What happened to
"I can do all things"?


01:09:10.012 --> 01:09:11.070
Why?


01:09:12.681 --> 01:09:14.444
Why did this happen?


01:09:16.585 --> 01:09:18.678
Why did I have to
lose everything?


01:09:18.754 --> 01:09:21.279
You didn't lose
everything, Bethany.


01:09:22.191 --> 01:09:23.715
Not even close.


01:09:25.461 --> 01:09:29.022
That shark didn't kill you.
You're still here.


01:09:29.999 --> 01:09:31.728
You're still alive.


01:09:32.868 --> 01:09:35.063
With a family that loves you.


01:09:39.175 --> 01:09:40.870
What am I supposed to do now?


01:09:46.615 --> 01:09:47.604
I don't know.


01:09:49.185 --> 01:09:51.483
Then how am I supposed to know?


01:09:55.858 --> 01:09:58.292
When the time is right,
you'll know.


01:09:59.261 --> 01:10:02.162
Until then, you pray


01:10:04.533 --> 01:10:06.000
and you listen.


01:10:06.936 --> 01:10:08.426
Listen for what?


01:10:10.706 --> 01:10:12.469
For what comes next.


01:10:24.987 --> 01:10:26.318
SARAH: Okay, Lymar,
I hope you remembered


01:10:26.388 --> 01:10:28.413
your toothbrush
this time. Okay?


01:10:28.490 --> 01:10:29.889
Did you remember your socks?


01:10:29.959 --> 01:10:31.984
Because you are not
borrowing mine again.


01:10:32.061 --> 01:10:34.052
Could you pass these out?


01:10:34.964 --> 01:10:35.953
Bethany?


01:10:40.703 --> 01:10:41.931
Mind if I tag along?


01:10:44.006 --> 01:10:47.373
I'm sure we can scrounge up
something for you to do.


01:10:52.581 --> 01:10:53.570
Hey.


01:12:00.582 --> 01:12:02.015
(BLEATING)


01:12:13.962 --> 01:12:15.395
(CLUCKING)


01:12:17.333 --> 01:12:19.358
All right, guys, let's go!


01:12:30.813 --> 01:12:33.646
(ROSEMARY SHOUTING
INSTRUCTIONS IN FRENCH)


01:12:38.887 --> 01:12:40.047
Rosemary!


01:12:40.122 --> 01:12:42.682
Sarah!
Hey, thank you for coming.


01:12:43.058 --> 01:12:44.047
This is Bethany.


01:12:44.126 --> 01:12:46.959
Bethany, yeah, I've heard a lot about you.
I'm happy you're here.


01:12:48.030 --> 01:12:49.725
Grab some bags
and pass them out.


01:12:49.798 --> 01:12:52.130
All right,
everybody make a line.


01:12:52.201 --> 01:12:54.897
Just grab it and pass it down.
Come on.


01:12:55.237 --> 01:12:56.932
Keep it going!
Come on guys.


01:12:57.005 --> 01:12:58.973
Keep going.
Make a line.


01:12:59.041 --> 01:13:00.269
Got it?


01:13:02.478 --> 01:13:03.740
Good job.


01:13:10.719 --> 01:13:12.880
(CHATTERING IN THAI)


01:13:12.955 --> 01:13:15.355
She wants to thank you all
for what you've been doing.


01:13:15.424 --> 01:13:16.482
They're very grateful.


01:13:16.558 --> 01:13:19.527
We're so happy we can help, we
know they've been through so much.


01:13:19.595 --> 01:13:21.825
(ROSEMARY TRANSLATING IN THAI)


01:13:21.897 --> 01:13:23.228
(WOMAN CHATTERING)


01:13:23.699 --> 01:13:26.566
ROSEMARY: She says it was just
a normal day like any other.


01:13:27.503 --> 01:13:29.471
But that they saw
the water roll back


01:13:29.538 --> 01:13:32.063
and they went to get the
fish and the lobsters.


01:13:32.641 --> 01:13:35.610
But then they saw the wave
and it was too late.


01:13:36.011 --> 01:13:38.605
And the water just kept coming,
there weren't many survivors.


01:13:40.449 --> 01:13:42.076
WOMAN: (CRYING)
I lost my family.


01:13:43.952 --> 01:13:46.477
Another family,
they all died...


01:13:52.494 --> 01:13:53.756
I'm so sad.


01:14:08.544 --> 01:14:09.806
You okay?


01:14:11.213 --> 01:14:12.339
Yeah.


01:14:13.115 --> 01:14:16.607
It's all right, don't be sorry
for compassion, Bethany.


01:14:17.219 --> 01:14:19.585
It can move us
to do amazing things.


01:14:19.955 --> 01:14:22.890
And it can help you
get a new perspective.


01:14:23.725 --> 01:14:25.215
Why don't you take a minute,


01:14:25.294 --> 01:14:27.626
then when you're feeling
better, come back and join us.


01:14:27.696 --> 01:14:29.994
'Cause there's
a lot to do. Okay?


01:14:30.065 --> 01:14:31.054
Good.


01:14:32.067 --> 01:14:33.466
(SNIFFLING)


01:14:51.620 --> 01:14:52.814
BETHANY: Here you go.


01:14:52.888 --> 01:14:55.049
(BETHANY SPEAKING IN THAI)


01:14:55.123 --> 01:14:56.112
Hello.


01:15:11.273 --> 01:15:12.331
Here you go.


01:15:14.510 --> 01:15:15.772
How come no one's in the water?


01:15:15.844 --> 01:15:17.141
We brought all these boards.


01:15:17.212 --> 01:15:18.338
Still petrified.


01:15:18.981 --> 01:15:20.812
Is it safe?
Yeah.


01:15:24.953 --> 01:15:26.215
Oh! (CHUCKLES)


01:15:26.288 --> 01:15:28.449
Something's missing, yeah?


01:15:28.524 --> 01:15:31.960
They said he wandered up a
few days after the tsunami.


01:15:32.027 --> 01:15:33.016
What's his name?


01:15:33.095 --> 01:15:34.460
They don't know.


01:15:34.530 --> 01:15:36.930
He hasn't said a word,
he won't even smile.


01:15:40.936 --> 01:15:43.461
Hey, do you want
to go in the water?


01:15:45.107 --> 01:15:48.167
Do you want to go out to
the ocean and go swimming?


01:15:48.243 --> 01:15:49.267
No?


01:16:02.291 --> 01:16:03.451
Hey, can I borrow your board?


01:16:03.525 --> 01:16:04.822
Yeah.


01:16:06.628 --> 01:16:07.959
BETHANY: Thank you.


01:16:10.399 --> 01:16:11.388
Thanks.


01:17:40.288 --> 01:17:41.687
(INAUDIBLE)


01:18:08.383 --> 01:18:10.908
BETHANY: They say the Lord
works in mysterious ways.


01:18:11.453 --> 01:18:13.819
I say that's an understatement.


01:18:13.889 --> 01:18:16.323
Who would have thought
that teaching a kid to surf


01:18:16.391 --> 01:18:18.018
would teach me
that surfing isn't


01:18:18.093 --> 01:18:20.493
the most important
thing in the world?


01:18:20.562 --> 01:18:22.826
And that something else is.


01:18:22.898 --> 01:18:23.990
Love.


01:18:24.332 --> 01:18:26.129
Bigger than any tidal wave.


01:18:26.201 --> 01:18:28.328
More powerful than any fear.


01:18:28.704 --> 01:18:30.501
(EXCITED CHATTERING)


01:18:33.175 --> 01:18:34.437
Hey, I'm home!


01:18:34.509 --> 01:18:35.635
Hey, there she is.


01:18:35.711 --> 01:18:36.700
How was your trip?


01:18:36.778 --> 01:18:37.767
BETHANY: Great.


01:18:37.846 --> 01:18:39.438
What's all this stuff?


01:18:39.514 --> 01:18:41.914
NOAH: Oh, you know,
just a little fan mail.


01:18:41.983 --> 01:18:43.883
Went ahead and sorted
it out by country.


01:18:43.952 --> 01:18:45.817
Are you serious?
Yup.


01:18:46.321 --> 01:18:49.882
And apparently, you are
very popular in Madagascar.


01:18:49.958 --> 01:18:51.118
No way.


01:18:51.193 --> 01:18:53.491
"Dear Bethany.
My name is Stephanie Bolt,


01:18:53.562 --> 01:18:55.621
"I'm 11 years old
and I go to Northcross


01:18:55.697 --> 01:18:57.688
"Intermediate School
in New Zealand."


01:18:57.766 --> 01:18:59.290
BETHANY:
People are so amazing.


01:18:59.501 --> 01:19:02.470
There's an eighth grader from
North Carolina, who lost his arm.


01:19:03.371 --> 01:19:05.999
Logan, and he says
he's gonna try out


01:19:06.074 --> 01:19:08.133
for his school soccer
team because of me.


01:19:09.177 --> 01:19:12.237
And he's rooting for me
in my next competition.


01:19:13.648 --> 01:19:14.706
I mean, I don't understand,


01:19:14.783 --> 01:19:16.910
I totally blew it at regionals.


01:19:16.985 --> 01:19:18.577
Why would they
want me to compete?


01:19:20.021 --> 01:19:21.352
You tried.


01:19:22.624 --> 01:19:26.924
And apparently, Dylan and
Stephanie like that.


01:19:37.739 --> 01:19:40.333
Hey, Dad.
I need your help.


01:19:42.344 --> 01:19:43.333
Name it.


01:19:43.411 --> 01:19:45.743
I think I want to compete.


01:19:47.983 --> 01:19:49.211
You sure?


01:19:50.652 --> 01:19:51.676
You don't have to.


01:19:51.987 --> 01:19:53.181
I'll take it heat by heat.


01:19:56.391 --> 01:19:57.483
Okay.


01:19:57.959 --> 01:20:00.393
So we need to
figure out something.


01:20:00.462 --> 01:20:02.987
Some way so when I duck
dive, I don't get pounded.


01:20:03.832 --> 01:20:04.821
Yeah.


01:20:07.502 --> 01:20:11.165
You mean something like this?


01:20:16.411 --> 01:20:17.400
Yeah.


01:20:32.894 --> 01:20:34.623
(CHEERING)


01:20:41.169 --> 01:20:43.000
You sure she can
use it in competition?


01:20:43.071 --> 01:20:45.335
Sure. Judges don't score on
how you get out to the waves.


01:20:45.407 --> 01:20:48.308
They only care what you
do when you catch one.


01:20:51.413 --> 01:20:53.438
Go ahead, say it.


01:20:53.949 --> 01:20:55.177
(LAUGHING)


01:20:55.784 --> 01:20:56.842
I'm a genius.


01:20:57.752 --> 01:20:59.151
You are...
Come on, say it.


01:20:59.654 --> 01:21:01.121
Tom, you're a genius!


01:21:01.189 --> 01:21:03.157
Genius.
You're very smart.


01:21:04.192 --> 01:21:05.955
Genius.
Come on, you know it.


01:21:06.027 --> 01:21:07.756
You're cute. You're very cute.
Genius. Genius.


01:21:09.397 --> 01:21:10.421
Hey.
Hey.


01:21:10.498 --> 01:21:11.965
Remember me?
No.


01:21:12.367 --> 01:21:15.302
That's really nice.
Best friends since birth, nothing.


01:21:15.370 --> 01:21:16.928
No. Nothing.
Good. Good sign.


01:21:17.005 --> 01:21:18.233
(BOTH LAUGHING)


01:21:18.306 --> 01:21:19.739
Hey, thanks for coming.


01:21:19.808 --> 01:21:21.537
Thanks for calling.


01:21:22.978 --> 01:21:24.639
I'm sorry I snapped
at you at regionals.


01:21:24.713 --> 01:21:25.702
Me, too.


01:21:26.815 --> 01:21:28.373
I miss you.
Me, too.


01:21:29.718 --> 01:21:31.549
Friends?
Of course.


01:21:31.853 --> 01:21:32.945
(LAUGHING)


01:21:33.722 --> 01:21:35.690
(IT'S YOUR LIFE PLAYING)


01:21:54.075 --> 01:21:55.201
(INAUDIBLE)


01:22:25.540 --> 01:22:26.529
KEOKI: Hey, Bethany!


01:22:27.842 --> 01:22:31.437
I saw you surfing out there this morning.
You were amazing.


01:22:31.513 --> 01:22:32.878
Maybe for a girl with one arm.


01:22:32.948 --> 01:22:34.279
By any standard.


01:22:34.349 --> 01:22:36.715
As for one arm, that just
levels the playing field.


01:22:36.785 --> 01:22:38.878
All right, all right.
What do you want?


01:22:39.421 --> 01:22:40.945
I want you to dominate
at nationals.


01:22:45.060 --> 01:22:47.620
Hey, Keoki, thanks.


01:22:48.663 --> 01:22:49.925
For what?


01:22:50.098 --> 01:22:52.794
Just for always showing up
for me, no matter what.


01:22:52.867 --> 01:22:54.596
Well, it's because
I care about you.


01:22:55.103 --> 01:22:57.367
I mean, even if you did miss
my last competition and all.


01:22:57.439 --> 01:22:59.168
I was in the hospital
you psycho.


01:22:59.240 --> 01:23:00.400
Excuses, excuses.


01:23:01.943 --> 01:23:03.274
Ah! Ow!


01:23:03.345 --> 01:23:05.074
Bethany, I'm sorry.
I wasn't even...


01:23:05.146 --> 01:23:06.135
Gotcha.


01:23:08.116 --> 01:23:09.378
BETHANY: Sucker!


01:23:10.518 --> 01:23:14.045
Welcome to the Rip Curl Junior
Nationals Surfing Championship.


01:23:14.122 --> 01:23:16.022
David Stanfield
along with Bo Hodge.


01:23:16.091 --> 01:23:17.922
And, Bo, we have
an exciting day today.


01:23:18.126 --> 01:23:20.594
BO: We've got an excellent
day of surfing on hand.


01:23:20.662 --> 01:23:23.324
We're going to see the best amateur
surfers from around the country today.


01:23:23.398 --> 01:23:25.457
DAVID: We have a panel of
four international judges


01:23:25.533 --> 01:23:27.091
watching this
national championship.


01:23:27.168 --> 01:23:28.465
High and low scores
are thrown out,


01:23:28.536 --> 01:23:30.504
but what are the judges
exactly looking for?


01:23:30.572 --> 01:23:32.301
Well, Dave,
we have 25-minute heats.


01:23:32.374 --> 01:23:35.309
Each rider is allowed to catch a
maximum of 10 waves per heat.


01:23:35.377 --> 01:23:37.902
The best two waves will be
tallied up for the final score.


01:23:37.979 --> 01:23:39.412
What the judges
are looking for:


01:23:39.481 --> 01:23:42.814
Style, flow and power and
control in radical maneuvers


01:23:42.884 --> 01:23:44.545
in the most critical
sections of the wave.


01:23:44.753 --> 01:23:46.618
Well, we have surf in the
six-to-eight-foot range,


01:23:46.688 --> 01:23:47.677
it looks like out there.


01:23:47.756 --> 01:23:49.553
What's key about
this six person heat


01:23:49.624 --> 01:23:52.024
is in fact that paddling
and positioning, right?


01:23:53.361 --> 01:23:56.091
These girls are tough, especially
Malina, you know that.


01:23:56.631 --> 01:23:57.962
The surf is big
out there today,


01:23:58.033 --> 01:23:59.557
so if you try to match
them wave for wave,


01:23:59.634 --> 01:24:01.534
you're just doing to wear yourself
out with all that paddling.


01:24:01.603 --> 01:24:02.695
Yeah.


01:24:02.771 --> 01:24:04.864
So don't take just any
wave that comes along.


01:24:05.774 --> 01:24:09.505
The greatest surfers, they
all have this sixth sense.


01:24:09.778 --> 01:24:11.939
They know when the
best waves are coming.


01:24:12.013 --> 01:24:14.243
They can feel it.
It's a gift.


01:24:15.483 --> 01:24:16.916
You have that gift, too.


01:24:16.985 --> 01:24:18.077
I do?


01:24:19.087 --> 01:24:21.180
Well, your mom's right, honey.
You are a little mermaid.


01:24:24.092 --> 01:24:28.461
You know that moment between
the sets when it's quiet


01:24:29.431 --> 01:24:31.058
and the waves haven't
even formed yet,


01:24:31.132 --> 01:24:33.100
it's just energy surging
through the water.


01:24:35.870 --> 01:24:37.497
Well, that's the time
to be patient.


01:24:39.174 --> 01:24:40.664
Listen to your instinct.


01:24:41.709 --> 01:24:42.698
Trust it.


01:24:45.380 --> 01:24:46.779
You'll know.


01:24:48.583 --> 01:24:49.607
Go get 'em.


01:24:49.851 --> 01:24:51.546
REPORTERS: Malina! Malina!


01:24:51.619 --> 01:24:54.782
Over the past few months, Malina Birch
has dominated every heat she's surfed


01:24:54.856 --> 01:24:56.721
winning three
contests in a row.


01:24:56.791 --> 01:24:59.487
No one has come close.
She's by far the person to beat today.


01:24:59.627 --> 01:25:00.855
(CLAMORING)


01:25:01.062 --> 01:25:02.461
REPORTERS: Bethany! Bethany!
(CAMERAS CLICKING)


01:25:02.530 --> 01:25:04.395
Don't worry, it's all
part of being sponsored.


01:25:04.466 --> 01:25:06.434
We love you, Bethany!
(WHOOPS)


01:25:06.734 --> 01:25:08.361
I'm going to go
get the rash guards.


01:25:11.039 --> 01:25:12.028
What are you doing here?


01:25:12.674 --> 01:25:14.539
I'm surfing, same as you.


01:25:14.676 --> 01:25:16.473
Well, I hope you don't
need to be rescued again.


01:25:17.445 --> 01:25:19.572
Actually, Malina,
I wanted to thank you.


01:25:20.081 --> 01:25:21.343
For what?


01:25:21.616 --> 01:25:24.483
Just for never taking it easy on me.
It means a lot.


01:25:26.221 --> 01:25:27.210
ALANA: You ready?


01:25:28.089 --> 01:25:29.181
Okay.


01:25:31.326 --> 01:25:33.294
DAVID: Bethany Hamilton's
appearance here


01:25:33.361 --> 01:25:35.295
is truly a remarkable comeback.


01:25:35.363 --> 01:25:38.025
Against all odds,
she has earned her spot


01:25:38.099 --> 01:25:39.964
into the National
Championships.


01:25:40.034 --> 01:25:41.524
Everyone in
attendance is hopeful


01:25:41.603 --> 01:25:43.571
that Bethany has
a great contest.


01:25:43.638 --> 01:25:47.438
But at the highest level of
competition, there are no free rides.


01:25:47.509 --> 01:25:49.272
We begin with our first
round of competition.


01:25:49.344 --> 01:25:50.402
(TOOTING)


01:25:50.478 --> 01:25:51.877
And there's the horn.
The first heat is underway.


01:26:00.855 --> 01:26:02.015
Yes!


01:26:07.529 --> 01:26:08.655
(CHEERING)


01:26:08.730 --> 01:26:09.719
Yes!


01:26:21.543 --> 01:26:22.601
(WHOOPING)


01:26:31.719 --> 01:26:32.845
(CHEERING)


01:26:49.971 --> 01:26:51.165
Can you believe that?


01:26:56.678 --> 01:26:57.770
(HORN SOUNDS)


01:26:57.845 --> 01:27:00.245
DAVID: Advancing into the
finals by 2/10's of a point,


01:27:00.315 --> 01:27:02.408
the big story is
Bethany Hamilton.


01:27:02.483 --> 01:27:06.044
She was looking for a 7.2 and
scored a 7.4 on her last wave.


01:27:06.454 --> 01:27:07.978
She'll be wearing blue
out in the lineup


01:27:08.056 --> 01:27:10.650
with her good friend, wearing
pink, Alana Blanchard.


01:27:10.725 --> 01:27:12.989
And their competitors,
black, Malina Birch.


01:27:13.061 --> 01:27:17.054
Yellow, Leila Hurst. White, Nage
Melamed, and in orange Kelia Moniz.


01:27:17.131 --> 01:27:19.929
And the judges are looking for
some progressive surfing today.


01:27:20.001 --> 01:27:22.333
BO: That's right, Dave.
They'll have a 25-minute heat,


01:27:22.403 --> 01:27:23.927
be scored on 10 waves,


01:27:24.005 --> 01:27:26.200
but they'll keep their best
two waves for the final score


01:27:26.274 --> 01:27:27.969
on the zero to ten point range.


01:27:28.042 --> 01:27:30.203
And there's the horn
and the heat is underway.


01:27:42.523 --> 01:27:43.751
(APPLAUSE)


01:27:46.060 --> 01:27:47.118
Yeah!


01:27:47.195 --> 01:27:50.392
BO: There's Nage Melamed.
She scores two vertical turns,


01:27:50.465 --> 01:27:52.558
and the judges
give her a 6. 75,


01:27:52.634 --> 01:27:54.261
and what a great
start to this heat.


01:27:56.537 --> 01:27:59.165
DAVID: Alana Blanchard
picking up a set wave.


01:27:59.440 --> 01:28:01.101
Works her way down the line.


01:28:01.175 --> 01:28:03.439
Snaps a big turn off the top.


01:28:03.511 --> 01:28:07.709
Runs around her competitor
with an aggressive reentry.


01:28:07.782 --> 01:28:10.148
And pink cracks
the lip one more time.


01:28:10.218 --> 01:28:11.651
Great run, Alana!


01:28:12.487 --> 01:28:15.320
BO: Situation with fifteen
minutes remaining in the heat,


01:28:15.390 --> 01:28:19.326
surfer in orange, Kelia
Moniz, you have a 5.4.


01:28:19.794 --> 01:28:23.696
Surfer in white, Nage
Melamed, you have a 6. 75.


01:28:24.098 --> 01:28:25.827
Surfer in pink,
Alana Blanchard,


01:28:25.900 --> 01:28:27.561
you are in first
place with a 7.0.


01:28:27.635 --> 01:28:28.624
Way to go, Alana!


01:28:29.570 --> 01:28:30.559
Go!


01:28:36.711 --> 01:28:37.803
(ALL GROAN)


01:28:37.879 --> 01:28:42.145
DAVID: Bo, Hamilton goes down hard in
the impact zone, and she is struggling.


01:28:43.518 --> 01:28:45.884
That's okay.
You'll get another one!


01:28:46.087 --> 01:28:47.452
Stay in there,
stay in there, Bethany.


01:28:48.423 --> 01:28:49.447
DAVID: Take a look at this.


01:28:49.524 --> 01:28:52.960
We've got four competitors
scratching for this wave.


01:28:53.027 --> 01:28:55.757
And surfer in black
takes control of the peak.


01:28:55.830 --> 01:28:57.320
BO: Birch on the
nice take off.


01:28:57.398 --> 01:28:59.161
She sprays Bethany!


01:29:04.405 --> 01:29:05.736
Great off the top!


01:29:05.807 --> 01:29:07.069
(CHEERING)


01:29:09.177 --> 01:29:11.270
Birch snaps under the lip.


01:29:12.146 --> 01:29:14.205
Banks it off the white
water one more time.


01:29:14.282 --> 01:29:15.544
Man, she is on fire today.


01:29:15.616 --> 01:29:19.780
One away. Malina Birch has scored
a 9.25 according to the judges,


01:29:19.854 --> 01:29:21.412
and that is a high score.


01:29:21.489 --> 01:29:23.923
Now she is in the lead,
Blanchard in second.


01:29:23.991 --> 01:29:26.619
Melamed in third,
Leila Hurst in fourth,


01:29:26.694 --> 01:29:30.824
Bethany Hamilton is in fifth, and
in sixth right now is Moniz.


01:29:31.866 --> 01:29:35.393
BO: Hamilton with a stall
and goes over the falls.


01:29:36.571 --> 01:29:37.663
Is she going to be all right?


01:29:37.739 --> 01:29:39.798
It's okay. Everybody gets
caught every once in a while.


01:29:39.874 --> 01:29:40.863
She can handle it.


01:29:43.111 --> 01:29:45.238
BO: Precious time on the
clock right now, Dave.


01:29:45.313 --> 01:29:48.339
And it looks like Alana is paddling
into a big wave on the outside.


01:29:48.416 --> 01:29:51.943
DAVID: Ooh! And Alana Blanchard
takes a spill there, too.


01:29:52.019 --> 01:29:55.182
Ladies and gentlemen, Malina
Birch is up and riding again.


01:29:55.256 --> 01:29:57.690
This girl's a wave
magnet today, Bo.


01:29:57.759 --> 01:29:59.590
She certainly is in
rhythm with the ocean.


01:29:59.660 --> 01:30:02.254
Way above the pack here
in today's competition.


01:30:08.035 --> 01:30:11.163
Malina Birch has just scored
a 9.5 on her last wave.


01:30:11.239 --> 01:30:13.400
That is the highest
wave of the contest.


01:30:13.474 --> 01:30:14.873
She's going to need
two nine-plus waves


01:30:14.942 --> 01:30:16.569
to even come close
to catching Malina.


01:30:16.644 --> 01:30:17.941
She's got less
than five minutes.


01:30:18.179 --> 01:30:21.148
DAVID: With time winding down
and no waves on the horizon,


01:30:21.215 --> 01:30:24.082
our surfers are anxious
to get a final score.


01:30:24.152 --> 01:30:28.054
Look for the girls to scramble for any
solid wave before the hooter blows.


01:30:34.195 --> 01:30:36.163
Check this out,
ladies and gentlemen.


01:30:36.230 --> 01:30:37.822
There's some
energy out in back.


01:30:37.899 --> 01:30:40.925
Looks like the girls have spotted
something on the horizon.


01:30:41.002 --> 01:30:43.232
Paddle, Bethany.
Paddle hard.


01:30:46.174 --> 01:30:47.505
Bo, take a look at this.


01:30:47.575 --> 01:30:50.738
Birch and Hamilton
paddle-battle out the back.


01:30:51.212 --> 01:30:53.510
BO: And Hamilton really needs
to beat her to the inside.


01:30:53.581 --> 01:30:54.570
If she's got
a chance here today.


01:30:54.649 --> 01:30:55.946
Come on, Bethany,
stay ahead of her!


01:30:57.718 --> 01:30:59.709
Don't let up!
You got her!


01:31:02.123 --> 01:31:06.253
Unbelievable, Bo, all Malina's got
to do is block Bethany Hamilton


01:31:06.327 --> 01:31:10.559
from getting to the inside and
she's got this contest in the bag.


01:31:14.535 --> 01:31:15.832
(PANTING)


01:31:16.804 --> 01:31:17.828
Paddle hard!


01:31:19.307 --> 01:31:22.105
Birch is still blocking
Hamilton from the inside.


01:31:22.176 --> 01:31:24.406
I don't know how she's going
to catch this wave, Bo.


01:31:24.612 --> 01:31:25.601
Paddle!


01:31:25.680 --> 01:31:27.443
Dave, we've got a
paddle-battle to the outside.


01:31:27.515 --> 01:31:28.743
It's Birch.
It's Hamilton.


01:31:28.816 --> 01:31:29.976
(YELLING)


01:31:30.051 --> 01:31:31.177
She's got her on the ropes.


01:31:31.252 --> 01:31:34.050
Can Bethany catch the wave?
This is her last chance.


01:31:48.169 --> 01:31:49.158
Yes!
Yes!


01:31:51.072 --> 01:31:52.505
She's got the wave, David!


01:31:52.573 --> 01:31:55.303
This is the one she's been
waiting for all contest long.


01:31:55.376 --> 01:31:57.435
Absolutely unbelievable.


01:31:57.512 --> 01:31:59.946
Bethany Hamilton duck
dives under Malina Birch


01:32:00.014 --> 01:32:02.346
while Birch is still out there
looking for another ride.


01:32:11.192 --> 01:32:12.750
(CHEERING)


01:32:14.161 --> 01:32:15.856
Sick one, Bethany!
(WHOOPING)


01:32:16.130 --> 01:32:19.429
That was an unbelievable
ride by Bethany Hamilton.


01:32:19.700 --> 01:32:20.894
(CHEERING)


01:32:21.302 --> 01:32:22.394
(WHOOPING)


01:32:22.470 --> 01:32:24.233
The judges
give her a 9. 7.


01:32:24.305 --> 01:32:25.602
(CHEERING)


01:32:27.008 --> 01:32:28.270
It's the highest
score of the heat!


01:32:28.342 --> 01:32:29.331
Wow!


01:32:29.410 --> 01:32:30.502
But she's still fifth!
All right, guys,


01:32:30.578 --> 01:32:31.602
she needs one more, one more.


01:33:04.145 --> 01:33:06.739
Bethany Hamilton is paddling
outside the lineup.


01:33:06.814 --> 01:33:08.782
What does she see?


01:33:08.849 --> 01:33:11.147
I don't know, Dave, but no
one's been paddling out


01:33:11.218 --> 01:33:12.480
in that area
all during the contest.


01:33:12.553 --> 01:33:13.815
Why is she so far out?


01:33:13.888 --> 01:33:15.014
What, is she giving up?


01:33:15.489 --> 01:33:16.956
I don't know.


01:33:17.491 --> 01:33:19.254
She feels something.


01:33:24.498 --> 01:33:26.227
What are you doing?


01:33:26.300 --> 01:33:28.734
Dave, there's only one minute
remaining on the clock.


01:33:28.803 --> 01:33:30.464
It is dead flat.


01:33:30.538 --> 01:33:32.870
The contest
may be already over.


01:33:37.878 --> 01:33:39.072
Why is she stopping?


01:33:39.580 --> 01:33:40.569
There's nothing out there.


01:33:40.648 --> 01:33:41.637
Not yet.


01:33:42.049 --> 01:33:45.917
DAVID: Only 45 seconds on the clock
and no set waves on the horizon.


01:33:45.987 --> 01:33:48.421
This contest may be over, Bo.


01:33:56.230 --> 01:33:58.596
We are counting down
to end this final.


01:33:58.666 --> 01:34:01.100
Just 30 seconds
left on the clock.


01:34:09.210 --> 01:34:10.302
Big bomb on the outside.


01:34:12.813 --> 01:34:14.644
BO: Fifteen seconds
remaining.


01:34:14.715 --> 01:34:16.273
Everybody else
is too far inside.


01:34:16.784 --> 01:34:19.810
DAVID: The Rip Curl Nationals,
10 seconds to go!


01:34:19.887 --> 01:34:23.482
And there is Bethany Hamilton with
an amazing wave out the back.


01:34:23.557 --> 01:34:24.649
Will this be enough?


01:34:31.265 --> 01:34:33.460
She is paddling
and here comes the wave.


01:34:33.534 --> 01:34:34.523
(SOUNDING)


01:34:35.069 --> 01:34:36.331
She's taken the drop!


01:34:36.437 --> 01:34:37.631
(CHEERING)


01:35:35.463 --> 01:35:36.862
(APPLAUSE)


01:35:41.402 --> 01:35:45.099
An amazing barrel for Bethany Hamilton.
Perfect positioning.


01:35:45.172 --> 01:35:46.298
Was she up before the horn?


01:35:46.474 --> 01:35:47.702
They have to count it.


01:35:51.512 --> 01:35:52.945
(CHEERING)


01:35:54.148 --> 01:35:55.706
Way to go, Bethany!


01:35:55.783 --> 01:35:56.772
Yeah!


01:36:07.461 --> 01:36:08.723
(SIGHS)


01:36:24.678 --> 01:36:27.044
Unbelievable.
Bethany Hamilton's


01:36:27.114 --> 01:36:29.241
amazing wave at the
end does not count.


01:36:29.316 --> 01:36:30.806
She stood up after the horn.
ALL: What?


01:36:30.885 --> 01:36:32.147
So she gets no score.


01:36:32.219 --> 01:36:34.483
Malina Birch,
your new National Champion.


01:36:34.555 --> 01:36:35.544
No!


01:36:36.190 --> 01:36:37.885
It's okay, Dad.
It's okay.


01:36:37.958 --> 01:36:38.947
But it didn't count.


01:36:39.760 --> 01:36:40.749
It counted.


01:36:42.730 --> 01:36:43.822
It totally counted.


01:36:46.700 --> 01:36:48.600
Yes, it did.


01:36:50.938 --> 01:36:52.838
I'm still checking
that video. Noah!


01:36:56.143 --> 01:36:57.735
(CAMERAS CLICKING)


01:37:03.184 --> 01:37:05.152
Hey. You okay?


01:37:05.219 --> 01:37:06.243
Very. Are you?


01:37:06.320 --> 01:37:07.309
Yeah.


01:37:08.155 --> 01:37:09.144
Yeah, I think so.


01:37:11.292 --> 01:37:12.418
What am I supposed to do now?


01:37:14.795 --> 01:37:18.253
You're supposed to
enjoy it. All of it.


01:37:18.999 --> 01:37:21.092
For the rest of your life.


01:37:27.274 --> 01:37:28.298
(CHEERING)


01:37:28.375 --> 01:37:31.708
DAVID: In fifth place, Bethany Hamilton!
Good job.


01:37:32.012 --> 01:37:33.240
Yeah! Bethany!


01:37:33.314 --> 01:37:36.078
And in fourth place,
Leila Hurst.


01:37:36.417 --> 01:37:38.851
Third place, Nage Melamed.


01:37:39.587 --> 01:37:41.953
Second place, Alana Blanchard.


01:37:42.022 --> 01:37:43.011
HOLT: Way to go, baby!


01:37:43.257 --> 01:37:46.385
And in first place,
Malina Birch.


01:37:51.332 --> 01:37:52.731
Hey.


01:37:52.800 --> 01:37:55.428
Hey, Malina. Great job.


01:37:55.502 --> 01:37:56.628
You're a tough opponent.


01:37:57.171 --> 01:38:00.629
Bethany Hamilton,
nobody is as tough as you.


01:38:02.509 --> 01:38:04.170
Get up here.
Come on. Come on.


01:38:06.113 --> 01:38:08.445
I'd like to share this win
with Bethany Hamilton.


01:38:08.949 --> 01:38:11.440
Because the judges may not
have counted that last wave,


01:38:12.419 --> 01:38:13.750
but I did.


01:38:14.889 --> 01:38:16.083
Bethany.


01:38:16.156 --> 01:38:17.350
(CHEERING)


01:38:25.099 --> 01:38:26.088
Bethany! Bethany!


01:38:26.166 --> 01:38:28.259
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Just back off, okay.


01:38:28.535 --> 01:38:30.400
It's okay.
Are you sure?


01:38:30.838 --> 01:38:32.396
You don't have to talk to them.


01:38:32.473 --> 01:38:36.170
Yeah, but what about Dylan
or Logan or Stephanie?


01:38:36.243 --> 01:38:37.870
What if they're watching?


01:38:37.945 --> 01:38:40.505
Bethany, I'm from
Transworld Surf magazine.


01:38:40.581 --> 01:38:42.208
Are you upset
you didn't win today?


01:38:42.283 --> 01:38:44.683
I didn't come to win.
I came to surf.


01:38:44.752 --> 01:38:46.344
Bethany, I just
wanted to ask you


01:38:46.420 --> 01:38:48.684
if you could go
back to that day


01:38:48.756 --> 01:38:50.917
and not have gone surfing,
would you do it?


01:38:54.161 --> 01:38:56.527
I wouldn't change
what happened to me,


01:38:56.597 --> 01:39:00.931
because then I wouldn't have this
chance in front of all of you.


01:39:01.769 --> 01:39:04.397
This chance to
embrace more people


01:39:04.471 --> 01:39:06.268
than I ever could
have with two arms.


01:39:17.651 --> 01:39:19.516
BETHANY: I was born to surf.


01:39:19.586 --> 01:39:22.953
This is why I wake up at the
crack of dawn every day.


01:39:23.023 --> 01:39:25.548
This is why I endure
belly rashes, reef cuts,


01:39:25.626 --> 01:39:28.424
muscles so tired
they feel like noodles.


01:39:29.129 --> 01:39:31.962
And I've learned that
life is a lot like surfing.


01:39:32.032 --> 01:39:35.763
When you get caught in the impact
zone, you need to get right back up


01:39:35.836 --> 01:39:38.464
because you never know
what's over the next wave.


01:39:38.639 --> 01:39:42.268
And if you have faith,
anything is possible.


01:39:42.343 --> 01:39:43.935
Anything at all.


01:39:44.011 --> 01:39:45.808
(THE UNKNOWN PLAYING)


01:40:17.378 --> 01:40:18.675
(CHEERING)


01:40:35.329 --> 01:40:37.160
Yeah, it was so much
fun just seeing him


01:40:37.231 --> 01:40:38.994
get better and better
on every wave


01:40:39.066 --> 01:40:42.832
and get up and ride all the way to the beach.
It was awesome.


01:40:42.970 --> 01:40:45.097
ANNOUNCER: Throwing out
the ceremonial first pitch


01:40:45.172 --> 01:40:49.302
of the 2004 season
is Bethany Hamilton.


01:40:49.376 --> 01:40:50.900
(CROWD ROARING)


01:40:53.313 --> 01:40:54.302
Strike.


01:40:55.349 --> 01:40:56.373
Thank you, Bethany!


01:40:59.620 --> 01:41:03.021
I think I got my courage
from Jesus Christ.


01:41:03.090 --> 01:41:04.819
He says, "Be strong."


01:41:12.766 --> 01:41:14.529
You think you're
going to surf again?


01:41:14.601 --> 01:41:16.125
I think?


01:41:16.203 --> 01:41:18.967
I know I'm going to surf again.


01:43:33.607 --> 01:43:35.871
(SET THE WORLD ON FIRE PLAYING)

